         <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">occupation</td>\n                <td class="p-2">Fisher</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">daily_routine</td>\n                <td class="p-2">Working adult</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">hobbies</td>\n                <td class="p-2">Ohangla dancing</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">activities</td>\n                <td class="p-2">Socialising with family or friends</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">health_conditions</td>\n                <td class="p-2">None of the above</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">medication</td>\n                <td class="p-2">Insulin injections, Oral medication (e.g., Metformin), Lifestyle changes only (no medication), Herbal or traditional medicine</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">healthcare_resources</td>\n                <td class="p-2">Local healthcare clinic or hospital</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">healthcare_access</td>\n                <td class="p-2">Yes</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">healthcare_frequency</td>\n                <td class="p-2">Regularly (at least once a year)</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">culture</td>\n                <td class="p-2">Luo</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">t2d_status</td>\n                <td class="p-2">Yes</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">tobacco</td>\n                <td class="p-2">No</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">alcohol</td>\n                <td class="p-2">Yes</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">physical_activity</td>\n                <td class="p-2">1-2 days</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">diet_restrictions</td>\n                <td class="p-2">Halal</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">support_network</td>\n                <td class="p-2">Family (parents, siblings, children)</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">Question</td>\n                <td class="p-2">Eating healthy can get expensive—how can I manage a nutritious diet on a tight budget? And can I still enjoy some traditional foods? </td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">generated_queries</td>\n                <td class="p-2">[\n  &quot;What are the best exercise routines for women aged 25-34 with type 2 diabetes living in urban areas of Siaya, Kenya?&quot;,\n  &quot;Are there any Ohangla dance groups or classes in Siaya town suitable for adults looking to increase physical activity for better health?&quot;,\n  &quot;What types of fish commonly caught in Lake Victoria are healthiest for someone with type 2 diabetes in the Luo culture?&quot;,\n  &quot;How do Luo dietary traditions in Siaya influence diabetes management, and what are recommended meal plans using locally available foods?&quot;,\n  &quot;Which local Apostolic Christian community wellness programs in Siaya support young women with diabetes?&quot;,\n  &quot;What challenges do urban fishers face in maintaining regular exercise routines in Siaya county?&quot;,\n  &quot;Are there any safe outdoor exercise spots in Siaya town for women, and what times are they less crowded?&quot;,\n  &quot;How does weekly alcohol consumption affect blood sugar control in women with type 2 diabetes who are moderately physically active?&quot;,\n  &quot;What are effective ways to integrate Ohangla dancing into a weekly fitness plan for managing diabetes?&quot;,\n  &quot;Where can I access diabetes support groups for young women in Siaya with easy access to healthy foods?&quot;,\n  &quot;Which local Luo herbal remedies are used alongside standard diabetes medication, and are they safe to combine with oral medications like Metformin?&quot;,\n  &quot;How can family support in a Luo context help improve exercise consistency and diabetes control for working women in urban Kenya?&quot;\n]</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">Category</td>\n                <td class="p-2">diet</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">study_number</td>\n                <td class="p-2">47514fc8-cb27-4dab-bf22-bf2c567de209</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">health_goals</td>\n                <td class="p-2">Eating healthy can get expensive—how can I manage a nutritious diet on a tight budget? And can I still enjoy some traditional foods? </td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">output_format</td>\n                <td class="p-2">Text, Image and audio</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">type</td>\n                <td class="p-2">overlapped</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">parent</td>\n                <td class="p-2"></td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">label</td>\n                <td class="p-2">EXCELLENT</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">story_arc</td>\n                <td class="p-2">social_support</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">output_tone</td>\n                <td class="p-2">social_support</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n                </tbody>\n            </table>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n     \n    <style>\n            .guideline-html-content h1 {\n                font-size: 1.1rem;\n                font-weight: 800;\n                margin-bottom: 0.5rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h2 {\n                font-size: 1rem;\n                font-weight: 700;\n                margin-bottom: 0.4rem;\n                margin-top: 1rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h3 {\n                font-size: 0.9rem;\n                font-weight: 600;\n                margin-bottom: 0.3rem;\n                margin-top: 0.8rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content p {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content ul,\n            .guideline-html-content ol {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n                padding-left: 1.25rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content li {\n                margin-bottom: 0.2rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content strong {\n                font-weight: 700;\n                color: #1e293b;\n            }\n        </style> </div> 	Most mornings, my day starts very early. I quickly brew some strong tea and grab oily mandazi from the kiosk because I’m in a hurry to the fish market by Lake Victoria. You’d think, eh, that with all the fish around, I’d eat healthy, but preparing omena or tilapia seems to take too long—and sometimes, with money for household things tight, buying those healthy vegetables like osuga just feels impossible! Last week, I forgot my Metformin pills, rushed to the cold market, and ended up feeling so dizzy that I almost dropped my basket full of dagaa before I could even sell. Have you ever wondered if small things like skipping a meal could spoil the whole day?\n\nLater that morning, a nurse at the local clinic saw me waiting outside while fanning myself, and she came to check on me. "Rose, you can still eat good Luo foods, but you must plan well," she said in that gentle voice. She explained, no need to buy expensive things—just grill or boil the fish, add mitoo or osuga, and make ugali with wimbi instead of white flour, so it won’t spike my sugar. She wrote down a simple meal plan and told me, "Next market day, buy leafy greens and try cooking with less oil. And join group walks if you can’t find Ohangla dancers—they are all exercise!" I wasn’t sure if all this would fit my busy life. Changing, even for health, is never easy, is it?\n\nThe next morning, I woke up early to prepare grilled tilapia with a big helping of steamed apoth before heading to the market. It was strange not frying things, and it made me want to sneak some mandazi later! I could hear my friends laughing that ‘Rose has forgotten how Luo women eat.’ I wanted to give up, but then I remembered this week we have the big community fishing contest. Wouldn’t I need enough strength to win if I stuck with the new meal plan and kept up my dancing? That thought kept me going, even if I slipped and had one small mandazi.\n\nStep by step, I found myself enjoying the new meals and having more energy at work. By the time of the fishing contest, my hands felt steady, and my feet were light enough to do a quick Ohangla step when I saw my friends cheering. We pulled out a net of fat tilapia, and I didn’t feel faint or dizzy. Even better, everyone wanted to taste my steamed omena! Now, I believe eating healthy the Luo way doesn’t cost more. I’m ready to keep learning, and maybe next week, I’ll be the one showing others this new style of living.	{https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/47514fc8-cb27-4dab-bf22-bf2c567de209_0.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/47514fc8-cb27-4dab-bf22-bf2c567de209_1.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/47514fc8-cb27-4dab-bf22-bf2c567de209_2.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/47514fc8-cb27-4dab-bf22-bf2c567de209_3.png}	{https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/47514fc8-cb27-4dab-bf22-bf2c567de209_0.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/47514fc8-cb27-4dab-bf22-bf2c567de209_1.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/47514fc8-cb27-4dab-bf22-bf2c567de209_2.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/47514fc8-cb27-4dab-bf22-bf2c567de209_3.mp3}	Eating healthy can get expensive—how can I manage a nutritious diet on a tight budget? And can I still enjoy some traditional foods? 	diet	female	overlapped	2026-02-24 14:11:10.203938+00	\N
