to talk. She asked why I skipped my morning walks and why I looked so tired. I shrugged, unsure. Margaret said, 'Nduta, even just 30 minutes of brisk walking, three or four days a week, can help your blood sugar and energy. You don’t need a gym – just a steady walk around your street will do. Think of it as time to talk to God or rehearse your stories.' It sounded so simple, but could it really work?\n\nI decided to try. I set my phone alarm each morning and told my cousin to look after the shop for a while. But it was tough! I was stiff after a few steps and every time I felt tired, I wanted to stop. I nearly gave up after feeling sore that Wednesday. But then I remembered – market day was coming and I had a lot more goods to carry than usual. I needed to be strong. I said, 'Let me just try one more day.'\n\nWith practice, those walks got easier! By Friday, my legs were less sore, and the walk even cleared my head. On market day, I moved my boxes and bags with less huffing and puffing than ever before. I finished stacking everything with a proud smile. Now, I wondered, what would happen if I keep this up? Maybe little habits, just repeated, are what make the big difference. Next week, I’ll walk again – who knows what else I can do!	{https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/1b6208f0-63ac-4762-b6a2-fe87a04fb857_0.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/1b6208f0-63ac-4762-b6a2-fe87a04fb857_1.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/1b6208f0-63ac-4762-b6a2-fe87a04fb857_2.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/1b6208f0-63ac-4762-b6a2-fe87a04fb857_3.png}	{https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/1b6208f0-63ac-4762-b6a2-fe87a04fb857_0.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/1b6208f0-63ac-4762-b6a2-fe87a04fb857_1.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/1b6208f0-63ac-4762-b6a2-fe87a04fb857_2.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/1b6208f0-63ac-4762-b6a2-fe87a04fb857_3.mp3}	How often and how long should I exercise to actually improve my health?	exercise	female	independent	2026-03-01 15:11:11.03774+00	\N
