acco</td>\n                <td class="p-2">Yes</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">alcohol</td>\n                <td class="p-2">No</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">physical_activity</td>\n                <td class="p-2">0 days</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">diet_restrictions</td>\n                <td class="p-2">Vegetarian</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">support_network</td>\n                <td class="p-2">Healthcare provider or counsellor</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">Question</td>\n                <td class="p-2">I like to snack—what are some healthy options and how often should I have them?</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">generated_queries</td>\n                <td class="p-2">[\n  &quot;What affordable and healthy snack options are available for someone living in rural Kiambu County with limited access to fresh foods and keeping kosher?&quot;,\n  &quot;How can a young male construction contractor in rural Kikuyu communities manage type 2 diabetes with frequent snacking and a busy work schedule?&quot;,\n  &quot;Are there any local Kikuyu traditional foods or snacks that fit a kosher diet and help regulate blood sugar levels for diabetes?&quot;,\n  &quot;Where can I buy or find healthy, diabetic-friendly snacks in small towns or rural centers in Kiambu County?&quot;,\n  &quot;What guidelines should someone who takes both insulin injections and oral medication follow for snacking throughout the workday?&quot;,\n  &quot;How do common social gatherings or Kikuyu rites and ceremonies in rural Kenya accommodate special dietary needs like kosher and diabetes management?&quot;,\n  &quot;What are the best ways to maintain diabetes management and snack healthily if I do not participate in physical activity during the week?&quot;,\n  &quot;Are there local support groups or healthcare providers in Kiambu County that offer nutrition counseling for young adult men with diabetes and limited food access?&quot;,\n  &quot;What are culturally acceptable ways to reduce unhealthy snacking during family or friend socialising among rural Kikuyu communities?&quot;,\n  &quot;How does weekly alcohol and tobacco use impact healthy snacking habits and blood sugar management for young men with type 2 diabetes in rural environments?&quot;,\n  &quot;Are there affordable ways to keep snacks fresh and safe to eat in rural areas with possible limited refrigeration, considering food safety for diabetic people?&quot;,\n  &quot;How often should someone of the Zion Christian Church faith, living in Kiambu, snack to support energy levels for construction work while managing type 2 diabetes?&quot;\n]</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">Category</td>\n                <td class="p-2">diet</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">study_number</td>\n                <td class="p-2">bc826419-0744-43cd-b6c8-245df3773c42</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">health_goals</td>\n                <td class="p-2">I like to snack—what are some healthy options and how often should I have them?</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">output_format</td>\n                <td class="p-2">Text, Image and audio</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">type</td>\n                <td class="p-2">independent</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">parent</td>\n                <td class="p-2"></td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">label</td>\n                <td class="p-2">GOOD</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">story_arc</td>\n                <td class="p-2">default</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">output_tone</td>\n                <td class="p-2">default</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n                </tbody>\n            </table>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n     \n    <style>\n            .guideline-html-content h1 {\n                font-size: 1.1rem;\n                font-weight: 800;\n                margin-bottom: 0.5rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h2 {\n                font-size: 1rem;\n                font-weight: 700;\n                margin-bottom: 0.4rem;\n                margin-top: 1rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h3 {\n                font-size: 0.9rem;\n                font-weight: 600;\n                margin-bottom: 0.3rem;\n                margin-top: 0.8rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content p {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content ul,\n            .guideline-html-content ol {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n                padding-left: 1.25rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content li {\n                margin-bottom: 0.2rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content strong {\n                font-weight: 700;\n                color: #1e293b;\n            }\n        </style> </div> 	One hot Tuesday, I was fixing the fence around Mama Wanjiku’s shamba. I had started work before breakfast and decided to have chai and some mandazi as my snack. Not even halfway into the job, my hands felt heavy, my mouth was dry, and my legs couldn’t hold me up well. I sat on a big stone, feeling a bit dizzy. The cows walked past, their bells ringing, and I wished I knew what went wrong. Isn’t it strange how small things like a snack can spoil your whole morning? That snack didn’t give me the energy I needed, and the work stopped for a long time until I felt better.\n\nLater that week, during my regular check-up at the village clinic, Nurse Njoki saw my blood sugar was not balanced. She looked at me with kind eyes and said, 'Mwangi, I know you love your snacks, but you must try healthier ones for your diabetes.' At first, I didn’t like the idea of changing my ways. But she explained slowly: 'Try carrot sticks, roasted groundnuts without much salt, boiled sweet potatoes, or some guavas when you get hungry. These are good for you and easy to find around here. Just have your snacks after a small meal, not all day. You’ll see the difference.' I nodded, still unsure—can small changes really help me finish my work strong?\n\nNext day, I packed roasted maize and sweet potato slices from home for my work. When my stomach started to rumble mid-morning, I remembered Nurse Njoki’s advice. I took a piece of sweet potato—tasted sweet but simple, not like mandazi! I missed the old taste, and by lunchtime, I almost bought chapati at the local duka. But then I remembered, I must finish fixing Mama Wanjiku’s new gate before the weekend. That thought kept me going, and I went back to the new snacks, slowly getting used to the change.\n\nSoon, my afternoons felt lighter, and I finished Mama Wanjiku’s fence and gate before Saturday. I even had energy left to join my family in singing ZCC songs after supper. Now, I look at snacks differently. I know I can choose better ones—like groundnuts and fruit—and I don’t need to snack all the time. With every good choice, my body feels ready for bigger tasks. Isn’t it good how a small snack can give you strength for both work and life? I’m ready for more improvements—one healthy snack at a time.	{https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/bc826419-0744-43cd-b6c8-245df3773c42_0.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/bc826419-0744-43cd-b6c8-245df3773c42_1.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/bc826419-0744-43cd-b6c8-245df3773c42_2.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/bc826419-0744-43cd-b6c8-245df3773c42_3.png}	{https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/bc826419-0744-43cd-b6c8-245df3773c42_0.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/bc826419-0744-43cd-b6c8-245df3773c42_1.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/bc826419-0744-43cd-b6c8-245df3773c42_2.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/bc826419-0744-43cd-b6c8-245df3773c42_3.mp3}	I like to snack—what are some healthy options and how often should I have them?	diet	male	independent	2026-03-01 15:11:07.910809+00	\N
