 in Kenya?&quot;,\n  &quot;Are there local support groups or resources in Kiambu for diabetic entrepreneurs living alone with limited social support?&quot;,\n  &quot;How can gardening as a hobby benefit my diabetes management, and what crops are best to grow in Kiambu urban areas for a healthy vegetarian diet?&quot;,\n  &quot;What are healthy vegetarian snack options that are also quick and convenient for someone with a busy work schedule in urban Kenya?&quot;,\n  &quot;How does regular access to urban healthcare clinics in Kiambu improve diabetes management compared to rural settings in Kenya?&quot;,\n  &quot;Are there culturally relevant dietary approaches within the Kikuyu community that help manage type 2 diabetes for vegetarians?&quot;,\n  &quot;What are the common challenges faced by working adults with diabetes who live alone in Kiambu, and how can they overcome them to maintain a healthy lifestyle?&quot;\n]</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">Category</td>\n                <td class="p-2">diet</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">study_number</td>\n                <td class="p-2">f8befec3-b257-434c-953c-586f59e193c0</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">health_goals</td>\n                <td class="p-2">Which everyday foods can I eat that won&#x27;t make my blood sugar spike?</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">output_format</td>\n                <td class="p-2">Text, Image and audio</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">type</td>\n                <td class="p-2">control</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">parent</td>\n                <td class="p-2"></td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">label</td>\n                <td class="p-2">EXCELLENT</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">story_arc</td>\n                <td class="p-2">resistance</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">output_tone</td>\n                <td class="p-2">resistance</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n                </tbody>\n            </table>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n     \n    <style>\n            .guideline-html-content h1 {\n                font-size: 1.1rem;\n                font-weight: 800;\n                margin-bottom: 0.5rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h2 {\n                font-size: 1rem;\n                font-weight: 700;\n                margin-bottom: 0.4rem;\n                margin-top: 1rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h3 {\n                font-size: 0.9rem;\n                font-weight: 600;\n                margin-bottom: 0.3rem;\n                margin-top: 0.8rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content p {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content ul,\n            .guideline-html-content ol {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n                padding-left: 1.25rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content li {\n                margin-bottom: 0.2rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content strong {\n                font-weight: 700;\n                color: #1e293b;\n            }\n        </style> </div> 	Every morning, I wake up in my flat in Kiambu and rush off with nothing but a mug of sweet tea and white bread. I light up a smoke as I check my phone for messages from clients, then, after a quick shower, I dash to my small shop down the busy street. If I remember, I grab a mandazi on my way and think, 'How can anything so sweet be bad when it makes work easier?' That day, I have to package vegetables for a customer’s order, but halfway, my hands start shaking, and I can't even focus on the stock numbers. I end up mixing up the orders. Is it really such a big deal to eat a little sugary snack if the work has to get done?\n\nLater that day, a nurse from the local clinic stops by—she's making rounds, handing out flyers on diabetes. I feel myself tense up. Surely, not another lecture? But she smiles and says, 'Kamau, you want energy, eh? Try boiled groundnuts, githeri with more beans than maize, even a ripe pawpaw or avocado for snacks. These won’t send your sugars jumping like mandazi.' She points to a bowl I left by the shop door. 'Swap that for some carrot sticks, you’ll still feel full!' Her words seem easy but her confidence makes me feel like maybe it won’t hurt to try them.\n\nThe next morning, I buy boiled groundnuts from Mama Mwangi at the junction instead of mandazi. It feels strange. I chew them, looking around to see if anyone notices. At lunchtime, I dish some githeri—less maize, more beans. But by midafternoon, my stomach still grumbles. I almost give up, thinking, maybe it’s easier to stick with what I know. But I remember tomorrow there’s a big delivery—worth more than double my usual orders. I decide to push through, telling myself, if this helps me finish strong, maybe it’s not so bad.\n\nThe delivery day arrives and, for once, I don’t feel so shaky or slow in the afternoon. I chop up carrot and cucumber for a snack and tuck them in my bag. Focusing is easier and when the client arrives, I check every box off with a clear mind. For the first time, I’m actually looking forward to eating sukuma wiki and some avocado at supper. Maybe if small changes can help with this big task, I can push for more healthy days ahead.	{https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/f8befec3-b257-434c-953c-586f59e193c0_0.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/f8befec3-b257-434c-953c-586f59e193c0_1.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/f8befec3-b257-434c-953c-586f59e193c0_2.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/f8befec3-b257-434c-953c-586f59e193c0_3.png}	{https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/f8befec3-b257-434c-953c-586f59e193c0_0.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/f8befec3-b257-434c-953c-586f59e193c0_1.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/f8befec3-b257-434c-953c-586f59e193c0_2.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/f8befec3-b257-434c-953c-586f59e193c0_3.mp3}	Which everyday foods can I eat that won't make my blood sugar spike?	diet	male	control	2026-03-01 15:11:09.751223+00	\N
