y traditions be incorporated into a healthy, gluten-free meal plan for a young woman with type 2 diabetes?&quot;,\n  &quot;What are practical strategies for quitting daily smoking tailored to young female commercial farmers in Kiambu?&quot;,\n  &quot;How frequently do urban healthcare clinics in Kiambu offer diabetes management workshops or nutritional counseling for women like me?&quot;,\n  &quot;What are some effective, culturally sensitive ways to talk about diabetes management with family members in a Kikuyu household?&quot;,\n  &quot;Where can I find educational resources or books about managing type 2 diabetes as a young, urban woman in Kenya?&quot;,\n  &quot;How can I adapt traditional Kikuyu dishes to be both gluten-free and suitable for diabetes, using locally sourced ingredients from Kiambu?&quot;\n]</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">Category</td>\n                <td class="p-2">diet</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">study_number</td>\n                <td class="p-2">7dc18ef3-c12f-4bc2-aa4e-51772be04468</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">health_goals</td>\n                <td class="p-2">Eating healthy can get expensive—how can I manage a nutritious diet on a tight budget? And can I still enjoy some traditional foods? </td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">output_format</td>\n                <td class="p-2">Text, Image and audio</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">type</td>\n                <td class="p-2">consistency</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">parent</td>\n                <td class="p-2">7b6469ac-643e-4eec-96c0-ab858a3b17b1</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">label</td>\n                <td class="p-2">EXCELLENT</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">story_arc</td>\n                <td class="p-2">social_support</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">output_tone</td>\n                <td class="p-2">social_support</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n                </tbody>\n            </table>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n     \n    <style>\n            .guideline-html-content h1 {\n                font-size: 1.1rem;\n                font-weight: 800;\n                margin-bottom: 0.5rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h2 {\n                font-size: 1rem;\n                font-weight: 700;\n                margin-bottom: 0.4rem;\n                margin-top: 1rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h3 {\n                font-size: 0.9rem;\n                font-weight: 600;\n                margin-bottom: 0.3rem;\n                margin-top: 0.8rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content p {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content ul,\n            .guideline-html-content ol {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n                padding-left: 1.25rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content li {\n                margin-bottom: 0.2rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content strong {\n                font-weight: 700;\n                color: #1e293b;\n            }\n        </style> </div> 	You know, sometimes I wake up when the sun is just peeking over the rooftops of Kiambu town, and right away start thinking, 'What jobs are waiting in my shamba today?' Most mornings, I rush out after swallowing whatever is quick – maybe just strong tea and bread from the kiosk. Then I work hard, moving fertilizer sacks and digging, with only a break when my stomach growls too much. One day, I decided to plant a whole patch of sukuma wiki before lunchtime. But my head started spinning, my hands got shaky, and I couldn't finish half my rows. How could such a simple farming job knock me down like that? I didn’t understand, but I just felt tired and defeated.\n\nLater that week, I went to the local clinic for my regular check-up and told the nurse, Agnes, about feeling dizzy and missing meals. She looked at me and smiled, 'Wanjiku, your body needs food like your farm needs rain. With diabetes, skipping meals or eating just bread can make you weak at the wrong time.' She gave me a meal plan, showed me millet porridge and boiled eggs for breakfast, and told me sukuma wiki and beans are even better than bread! She even said, 'Don’t worry, you don’t have to give up your favorites. Just cook them with more greens, less oil, and pick cheaper, local grains like sorghum and sweet potato.' I still doubted, 'Really? Can I afford all that and still work my shamba?'\n\nSo I tried. The next morning, I steamed some sweet potatoes and boiled an egg. It was not what I was used to, and it felt slow to prepare compared to my usual bread. Later, when my friends laughed at my 'healthy' meal, I almost wanted to give up. At lunchtime, I missed my snack because I was so busy in the shamba, and again felt shaky. But I remembered the nurse’s words and thought, 'There is that big order for kale next week, and I don’t want to let my family down.' So I tried again the next day – this time, packing groundnuts and a fruit in my bag.\n\nSlowly, the new routine got easier. After a few days, I found I could do more farm work without that heavy tiredness. Sweet potato porridge with avocado didn’t just fill me – it kept my energy steady all morning. By the time the big buyer came for kale, I was ready! My parents cheered as I loaded full sacks, and for the first time, I thought, 'Maybe these small changes really matter.' Now, I feel ready to keep learning and even share what I know with my church group. Who knew healthy eating could be this possible and still taste like home?	{https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/7dc18ef3-c12f-4bc2-aa4e-51772be04468_0.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/7dc18ef3-c12f-4bc2-aa4e-51772be04468_1.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/7dc18ef3-c12f-4bc2-aa4e-51772be04468_2.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/7dc18ef3-c12f-4bc2-aa4e-51772be04468_3.png}	{https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/7dc18ef3-c12f-4bc2-aa4e-51772be04468_0.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/7dc18ef3-c12f-4bc2-aa4e-51772be04468_1.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/7dc18ef3-c12f-4bc2-aa4e-51772be04468_2.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/7dc18ef3-c12f-4bc2-aa4e-51772be04468_3.mp3}	Eating healthy can get expensive—how can I manage a nutritious diet on a tight budget? And can I still enjoy some traditional foods? 	diet	female	consistency	2026-03-01 15:11:11.532276+00	\N
