th both kosher dietary practices and traditional Kikuyu herbal remedies for diabetes?&quot;,\n  &quot;What are effective ways for a busy working adult in Murangâ€™a with limited social support to avoid late-night eating triggers while balancing family social activities?&quot;,\n  &quot;Are there success stories from business owners in Murangâ€™a managing type 2 diabetes and hypertension without relying solely on medication?&quot;,\n  &quot;What practical meal-planning strategies can people in urban Murangâ€™a use to prepare healthy, early dinners with limited access to fresh foods?&quot;,\n  &quot;Which forms of gardening or urban farming are popular among older adults in Murangâ€™a for supplementing healthy diets for diabetes management?&quot;,\n  &quot;How can I integrate traditional Kikuyu dietary practices with a kosher diet to better control my late-night blood sugar spikes?&quot;\n]</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">Category</td>\n                <td class="p-2">exercise</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">study_number</td>\n                <td class="p-2">523e7d4a-7faa-484a-afb7-aa510b33a064</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">health_goals</td>\n                <td class="p-2">How often and how long should I exercise to actually improve my health?</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">output_format</td>\n                <td class="p-2">Text, Image and audio</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">type</td>\n                <td class="p-2">consistency</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">parent</td>\n                <td class="p-2">2d2e2931-4bad-48ad-97a5-84ebc0c46d1c</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">label</td>\n                <td class="p-2">EXCELLENT</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">story_arc</td>\n                <td class="p-2">social_support</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">output_tone</td>\n                <td class="p-2">social_support</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n                </tbody>\n            </table>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n     \n    <style>\n            .guideline-html-content h1 {\n                font-size: 1.1rem;\n                font-weight: 800;\n                margin-bottom: 0.5rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h2 {\n                font-size: 1rem;\n                font-weight: 700;\n                margin-bottom: 0.4rem;\n                margin-top: 1rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h3 {\n                font-size: 0.9rem;\n                font-weight: 600;\n                margin-bottom: 0.3rem;\n                margin-top: 0.8rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content p {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content ul,\n            .guideline-html-content ol {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n                padding-left: 1.25rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content li {\n                margin-bottom: 0.2rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content strong {\n                font-weight: 700;\n                color: #1e293b;\n            }\n        </style> </div> 	The other day, I closed my shop in Murang’a town quite late, around eight-thirty. I was tired, my feet ached, as usual. I got home and made some mukimo with potatoes and maize, plus a bit of cabbage—nothing fancy because sometimes getting fresh vegetables is expensive here. I ate quickly, just before nine, thinking, surely, food is food, and I must fill my stomach. But that night, I tossed in bed, feeling restless and sweating, my mind wandering—was it the late food? The next morning, I felt weak; work at the shop was hard. A delivery I had been waiting for arrived, but I muddled it up, mixing customer orders—how could a simple thing turn so upside down?\n\nLater in the week, I visited the local clinic for my regular check. The nurse, Mrs. Wanjiku, she looked at my numbers and asked, ‘Kamau, do you eat late at night?’ I hesitated. She smiled, ‘It’s common here in town, I know. But when you eat supper after 7 pm, especially starchy food, your sugar stays high all night. Try to finish your main meal before six if possible, and take a thirty-minute brisk walk, even inside your plot. That will help your body carry you through shop work and the farm on weekends. You don’t have to run. Just walk, move, even while listening to the news. Eh, what do you think?’ I grinned, still unsure if I could change, but her words sat with me.\n\nThe next evening, I cooked early, made some githeri with more beans than maize, like she suggested, though it took practice. At sunset, I put on my old blue sweater and tried a walk down the dusty road near my house, like Mrs. Wanjiku said. Eish, after ten minutes, my hips started complaining! I almost turned back, but then I thought, Kamau, remember that big market delivery next week—the one job that could grow the shop? So I kept walking, slow, but I finished. Even so, by bedtime, I missed my old routine: late TV and late-night tea.\n\nBy the next week, I was walking every evening, just after supper. It got easier—my feet hurt less, my legs felt lighter. When the market delivery day came, I was steadier, organised, and even happier. I didn’t confuse the orders this time. Maybe it was small, but I noticed—if I keep at this, the work will get easier, maybe life too. Who would have thought a simple walk could start to fix things?	{https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/523e7d4a-7faa-484a-afb7-aa510b33a064_0.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/523e7d4a-7faa-484a-afb7-aa510b33a064_1.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/523e7d4a-7faa-484a-afb7-aa510b33a064_2.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/523e7d4a-7faa-484a-afb7-aa510b33a064_3.png}	{https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/523e7d4a-7faa-484a-afb7-aa510b33a064_0.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/523e7d4a-7faa-484a-afb7-aa510b33a064_1.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/523e7d4a-7faa-484a-afb7-aa510b33a064_2.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/523e7d4a-7faa-484a-afb7-aa510b33a064_3.mp3}	How often and how long should I exercise to actually improve my health?	exercise	male	consistency	2026-03-01 15:11:10.340139+00	\N
