"p-2 font-bold">alcohol</td>\n                <td class="p-2">No</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">physical_activity</td>\n                <td class="p-2">3-4 days</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">diet_restrictions</td>\n                <td class="p-2">Halal</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">support_network</td>\n                <td class="p-2">Close friends</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">Question</td>\n                <td class="p-2">Which everyday foods can I eat that won&#x27;t make my blood sugar spike?</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">generated_queries</td>\n                <td class="p-2">[\n  &quot;What are some healthy, lactose-free snack options popular in Katsina city for someone managing type 2 diabetes?&quot;,\n  &quot;How does being a male Hausa Muslim grain merchant in urban Katsina influence recommended snack choices during Ramadan?&quot;,\n  &quot;Which locally available grains in Katsina can I use to make diabetes-friendly snacks?&quot;,\n  &quot;How often should a 25-34 year-old male with type 2 diabetes, who exercises 3-4 days a week, eat snacks to maintain stable blood sugar?&quot;,\n  &quot;Are there traditional Hausa snacks that are both lactose-free and suitable for people with diabetes?&quot;,\n  &quot;What are the best urban markets or stores in Katsina to find healthy, lactose-free snack ingredients?&quot;,\n  &quot;How can I incorporate my farming-related interests to prepare healthy snacks at home for my dietary needs?&quot;,\n  &quot;Are there any support groups in urban Katsina for young adults with diabetes to share snack ideas?&quot;,\n  &quot;What should I consider when choosing between Western and traditional Hausa snacks, given my need for lactose-free and diabetes-friendly foods?&quot;,\n  &quot;How might occasional tobacco and alcohol use interact with snacking habits for men with diabetes in urban Katsina?&quot;,\n  &quot;What local healthcare clinics in Katsina offer nutrition counseling specifically for diabetic merchants?&quot;,\n  &quot;How can I ensure my snacks meet Islamic dietary guidelines while helping manage my blood sugar and lactose intolerance in Hausa culture?&quot;\n]</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">Category</td>\n                <td class="p-2">diet</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">study_number</td>\n                <td class="p-2">a180d2f8-8cd3-4752-bc3e-9503d1ee2579</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">health_goals</td>\n                <td class="p-2">Which everyday foods can I eat that won&#x27;t make my blood sugar spike?</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">output_format</td>\n                <td class="p-2">Text, Image and audio</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">type</td>\n                <td class="p-2">independent</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">parent</td>\n                <td class="p-2"></td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">label</td>\n                <td class="p-2">EXCELLENT</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">story_arc</td>\n                <td class="p-2">resistance</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">output_tone</td>\n                <td class="p-2">resistance</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n                </tbody>\n            </table>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n     \n    <style>\n            .guideline-html-content h1 {\n                font-size: 1.1rem;\n                font-weight: 800;\n                margin-bottom: 0.5rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h2 {\n                font-size: 1rem;\n                font-weight: 700;\n                margin-bottom: 0.4rem;\n                margin-top: 1rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h3 {\n                font-size: 0.9rem;\n                font-weight: 600;\n                margin-bottom: 0.3rem;\n                margin-top: 0.8rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content p {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content ul,\n            .guideline-html-content ol {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n                padding-left: 1.25rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content li {\n                margin-bottom: 0.2rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content strong {\n                font-weight: 700;\n                color: #1e293b;\n            }\n        </style> </div> 	Every morning, I, Chinonso Okafor, get up before the call to prayer, do my ablution, and get ready for another busy day in my grain shop near the heart of Katsina city. You know, selling millet, sorghum, and maize to customers is no small job. I used to just grab whatever was easy for breakfast—a bowl of kunu if I had time, or sometimes even sweet tea with bread. I would munch on kulikuli or some roasted corn at the shop, not even thinking if it mattered. Who really has time to worry about blood sugar when the whole market is bustling, right? One day, though, my hands started shaking while lifting a sack of maize. I dropped it—right there in front of my friend Musa and a line of customers. Was it just tiredness, or could it be because of this sugar thing everyone talks about? Honestly, I felt embarrassed.\n\nLater that week, I visited the local clinic when my cousin insisted. The nurse, a calm woman named Hadiza, explained things in a simple way. "Chinonso, your work is important, but how will you carry those bags if your blood sugar keeps jumping up and down?" she smiled. I frowned, not so sure. She told me to try snacks like roasted groundnuts, tiger nuts (aya), or beans-based kosai during my break instead of sweet tea and kulikuli. She even wrote down a little list: roasted corn (no sugar), steamed moi moi, and to always check how much fruit I eat. Take small portions, she said. But honestly, how can groundnuts give energy like bread and sugary kunu, I thought?\n\nWell, I decided to try Hadiza's advice the next day. I measured out a handful of roasted groundnuts and packed some boiled sweet potato before heading to the shop. But my hand kept reaching for the sweet bread as I passed the tea stand. It's hard, you know! Was I really supposed to eat beans and nuts when everybody else is enjoying masa and sugar? The first few days, I even felt a bit grumpy and low on energy. Still, I remembered, the market boss had assigned me to supervise the new supply delivery soon. I couldn't let another mistake happen in front of everyone.\n\nSlowly, I noticed changes. My hands stopped shaking, and my energy started lasting longer, especially after breaking my fast with roasted groundnuts and tiger nuts on busy market days. When the big maize lorry arrived, I lifted the sacks easily and counted all my goods without feeling dizzy. Friends noticed, too—Musa even asked if I had joined the local football team! Now, I'm thinking, maybe Hadiza was right. Why not learn more snacks to keep me moving? After all, the market waits for no one!	{https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/a180d2f8-8cd3-4752-bc3e-9503d1ee2579_0.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/a180d2f8-8cd3-4752-bc3e-9503d1ee2579_1.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/a180d2f8-8cd3-4752-bc3e-9503d1ee2579_2.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/a180d2f8-8cd3-4752-bc3e-9503d1ee2579_3.png}	{https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/a180d2f8-8cd3-4752-bc3e-9503d1ee2579_0.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/a180d2f8-8cd3-4752-bc3e-9503d1ee2579_1.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/a180d2f8-8cd3-4752-bc3e-9503d1ee2579_2.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/a180d2f8-8cd3-4752-bc3e-9503d1ee2579_3.mp3}	Which everyday foods can I eat that won't make my blood sugar spike?	diet	male	independent	2026-02-22 22:58:58.220814+00	\N
