me inexpensive, culturally familiar snacks or small meals suitable for a Hausa Muslim female with diabetes to eat during work days?&quot;,\n  &quot;Where can I access nutrition counseling or tailored meal planning for diabetes and hypertension in or near Kano rural health clinics?&quot;,\n  &quot;How do other women traders in Hausa rural communities manage their blood pressure and sugar levels while balancing work and family life?&quot;,\n  &quot;Are there local Hausa storytelling traditions or social activities that encourage and support healthier eating habits and lifestyle change among women?&quot;,\n  &quot;What affordable meal prep ideas incorporate both traditional Hausa foods and dietary changes recommended for diabetes and hypertension in rural Nigeria?&quot;\n]</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">Category</td>\n                <td class="p-2">diet</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">study_number</td>\n                <td class="p-2">48b18430-56fd-4dea-b502-3775d584d35e</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">health_goals</td>\n                <td class="p-2">Which everyday foods can I eat that won&#x27;t make my blood sugar spike?</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">output_format</td>\n                <td class="p-2">Text, Image and audio</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">type</td>\n                <td class="p-2">independent</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">parent</td>\n                <td class="p-2"></td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">label</td>\n                <td class="p-2">BAD</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">story_arc</td>\n                <td class="p-2">classic_change</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">output_tone</td>\n                <td class="p-2">classic_change</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n                </tbody>\n            </table>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n     \n    <style>\n            .guideline-html-content h1 {\n                font-size: 1.1rem;\n                font-weight: 800;\n                margin-bottom: 0.5rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h2 {\n                font-size: 1rem;\n                font-weight: 700;\n                margin-bottom: 0.4rem;\n                margin-top: 1rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h3 {\n                font-size: 0.9rem;\n                font-weight: 600;\n                margin-bottom: 0.3rem;\n                margin-top: 0.8rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content p {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content ul,\n            .guideline-html-content ol {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n                padding-left: 1.25rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content li {\n                margin-bottom: 0.2rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content strong {\n                font-weight: 700;\n                color: #1e293b;\n            }\n        </style> </div> 	The other day, I was trying to finish my small bookkeeping work at home. I made a big pot of white rice and stew with plenty of oil for lunch—I thought, what could go wrong? My plan was to check my receipts and finish early, but after lunch I just felt heavy and tired. My eyes became blurry and I could not even finish counting the money. I ignored the feeling and tried to keep working. But why did I even feel so tired just after eating? Could my food be affecting my work?\n\nLater that week, Nurse Zanele from the clinic came for her home visit. I told her how I felt after eating, and she listened with a kind face. She said, 'Amina, you are not alone. Many foods can make your blood sugar go up fast, especially white rice and heavy oil. Try eating more brown rice, wholewheat bread, grilled chicken, beans, and lots of green veggies. Put less oil in your stew, and use lemon, ginger, and herbs to add flavour. This way, you will feel lighter and still enjoy your meals.' I nearly laughed! Could changing rice and using herbs really make such a difference?\n\nI tried to take her advice, but you know, change is not as simple as talking! I caught myself reaching for white bread and sweet tea out of old habit. Eish, my family even teased me when I served brown rice, asking, 'Amina, why is the rice brown today?' When the taste felt strange, I almost gave up. But I remembered the bigger job at the end of the week: hosting our family’s Friday lunch. I told myself, let me give this health thing one real chance.\n\nSlowly, my energy came back and I felt lighter after eating. When Friday arrived, I cooked grilled chicken with lots of green beans and brown rice. The food tasted good and everyone left the table full, laughing and surprised! Who knew? Even my family liked the change. I looked at my bookkeeping later that evening and finally finished without yawning once. Now I feel like, with small changes, I can care for my health and still do what I love. Maybe, just maybe, I am ready to learn more every day.	{https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/48b18430-56fd-4dea-b502-3775d584d35e_0.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/48b18430-56fd-4dea-b502-3775d584d35e_1.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/48b18430-56fd-4dea-b502-3775d584d35e_2.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/48b18430-56fd-4dea-b502-3775d584d35e_3.png}	{https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/48b18430-56fd-4dea-b502-3775d584d35e_0.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/48b18430-56fd-4dea-b502-3775d584d35e_1.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/48b18430-56fd-4dea-b502-3775d584d35e_2.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/48b18430-56fd-4dea-b502-3775d584d35e_3.mp3}	Which everyday foods can I eat that won't make my blood sugar spike?	diet	female	independent	2026-02-22 22:58:58.340257+00	\N
