td class="p-2 font-bold">disability</td>\n                <td class="p-2">I do not have a disability</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">occupation</td>\n                <td class="p-2">Trader</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">daily_routine</td>\n                <td class="p-2">Working adult</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">hobbies</td>\n                <td class="p-2">Cooking</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">activities</td>\n                <td class="p-2">Exercise or physical activities</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">health_conditions</td>\n                <td class="p-2">Less than 30 minutes per day</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">medication</td>\n                <td class="p-2">Oral medication (e.g., Metformin)</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">healthcare_resources</td>\n                <td class="p-2">Local healthcare clinic or hospital</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">healthcare_access</td>\n                <td class="p-2">Yes</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">healthcare_frequency</td>\n                <td class="p-2">Regularly (at least once a year)</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">t2d_status</td>\n                <td class="p-2">Yes</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">tobacco</td>\n                <td class="p-2">No</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">alcohol</td>\n                <td class="p-2">No</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">physical_activity</td>\n                <td class="p-2">5-7 days</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">diet_restrictions</td>\n                <td class="p-2">Halal</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">support_network</td>\n                <td class="p-2">I live alone or have limited support</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">Question</td>\n                <td class="p-2">I like to snack—what are some healthy options and how often should I have them?</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">generated_queries</td>\n                <td class="p-2">[\n  &quot;What at-home exercise routines are culturally appropriate and easy to do for a 25-34 year old Hausa woman living in suburban Kano with no gym access?&quot;,\n  &quot;Are there examples of effective physical activities using household items suitable for women traders in Kano who practice Islam and follow halal dietary restrictions?&quot;,\n  &quot;What are traditional Hausa exercises or dance forms in Kano that can help manage type 2 diabetes for women?&quot;,\n  &quot;What are some healthy and easy-to-cook halal meals that fit the typical schedule of a busy female trader in suburban Kano?&quot;,\n  &quot;How do local parks or open spaces in suburban Kano support women&#x27;s exercise routines, especially for those who exercise 5-7 days per week?&quot;,\n  &quot;What community resources or women&#x27;s groups in Kano support diabetic women with limited support networks who want to stay active?&quot;,\n  &quot;Are there safety considerations for women exercising outdoors in suburban areas near Kano, Nigeria, in the early morning or evening?&quot;,\n  &quot;What are Hausa-inspired ways to make football (soccer) part of a home or small-group workout routine for a woman living alone?&quot;,\n  &quot;What alternatives to Metformin are commonly used among Hausa women in Kano for type 2 diabetes management, considering herbal or traditional medicine options?&quot;,\n  &quot;How can a working adult female trader in Kano align regular physical activity with Islamic prayer times and fasting periods?&quot;,\n  &quot;Are there personal stories or advice from Hausa women in suburban Kano on maintaining a healthy lifestyle with diabetes and limited family support?&quot;,\n  &quot;What daily routines can help women traders in Kano balance their business, health (including diabetes), and exercise without relying on gyms?&quot;\n]</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">Category</td>\n                <td class="p-2">diet</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">study_number</td>\n                <td class="p-2">111ccc60-a30c-43c8-b927-249693d357f5</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">health_goals</td>\n                <td class="p-2">I like to snack—what are some healthy options and how often should I have them?</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">output_format</td>\n                <td class="p-2">Text, Image and audio</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">type</td>\n                <td class="p-2">consistency</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">parent</td>\n                <td class="p-2">33b80962-7269-4711-a426-524be2e00663</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">label</td>\n                <td class="p-2">EXCELLENT</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">story_arc</td>\n                <td class="p-2">social_support</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">output_tone</td>\n                <td class="p-2">social_support</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n                </tbody>\n            </table>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n     \n    <style>\n            .guideline-html-content h1 {\n                font-size: 1.1rem;\n                font-weight: 800;\n                margin-bottom: 0.5rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h2 {\n                font-size: 1rem;\n                font-weight: 700;\n                margin-bottom: 0.4rem;\n                margin-top: 1rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h3 {\n                font-size: 0.9rem;\n                font-weight: 600;\n                margin-bottom: 0.3rem;\n                margin-top: 0.8rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content p {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content ul,\n            .guideline-html-content ol {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n                padding-left: 1.25rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content li {\n                margin-bottom: 0.2rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content strong {\n                font-weight: 700;\n                color: #1e293b;\n            }\n        </style> </div> 	My name is Aisha Ibrahim. Every day, I wake up early in our small compound near Kano, put on my scarf, and get ready for a busy day at the market. As a trader, I rush to open my stall and stack my tomatoes and peppers before the customers come. I like to snack in between, usually some fried akara from across the road. I always think, how can a little snack be bad? That morning, I was hungry and tired and tried to sort my goods quickly, but my hands started shaking and I felt dizzy. I spilled a whole bowl of tomatoes, and my neighbour, Baba Sani, laughed, saying, 'Aisha, you dey rush too much!' It was just a small job, but I had to rest for a while before cleaning up my mess. I wondered, does food really control my energy this much?\n\nA few days later, I visited the local health clinic for my yearly checkup. Nurse Ngozi, in her white hijab, smiled as she saw my record with type 2 diabetes. She asked, 'Aisha, what do you snack on at work?' I shrugged, 'Just akara and groundnuts. Sometimes kuli-kuli too.' She nodded gently and explained, 'Try switching to small portions of roasted groundnuts, cucumber slices, or a boiled egg instead. They're all halal and easy to carry. Snack only the size of your palm, and wait at least two hours before taking more.' Honestly, I was not sure at first. Will this fill me up? But she said, 'You want to work well and feel strong, right? These healthy snacks help keep your sugar steady, especially with your medicine.' I promised to try.\n\nBack at the market, I prepared a bowl with cucumber sticks and some boiled groundnuts. When my stomach rumbled, I missed the taste of hot akara, but I remembered what Nurse Ngozi said. I took a slow breath and ate the cucumber. My friend Amina stopped by and pulled out suya bread to share. I almost took it, but I stopped myself. For a while, I felt awkward, like I was missing out. By midday, my energy dropped—I was not used to this new routine yet. But I kept on, because next week is Sallah festival and everyone expects me to organise the big vegetable order for the mosque. That thought gave me courage. Can I really change for good?\n\nEach day, I tried the new snacks, sometimes adding apple slices or okpa. It was not easy, but I noticed I was not so tired at the end of my market shift. My hands no longer shook, and I had more strength even during busy times. When festival week arrived, I managed all the mosque orders smoothly and even had time to help a neighbour set up her stall. Now, I feel proud of my progress. I am ready to keep learning about healthy options—maybe roasted plantain next—and stay strong for my work and life. Who knew small changes could help so much?	{https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/111ccc60-a30c-43c8-b927-249693d357f5_0.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/111ccc60-a30c-43c8-b927-249693d357f5_1.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/111ccc60-a30c-43c8-b927-249693d357f5_2.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/111ccc60-a30c-43c8-b927-249693d357f5_3.png}	{https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/111ccc60-a30c-43c8-b927-249693d357f5_0.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/111ccc60-a30c-43c8-b927-249693d357f5_1.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/111ccc60-a30c-43c8-b927-249693d357f5_2.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/111ccc60-a30c-43c8-b927-249693d357f5_3.mp3}	I like to snack—what are some healthy options and how often should I have them?	diet	female	consistency	2026-02-22 22:58:58.610018+00	\N
