</td>\n                <td class="p-2">No</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">physical_activity</td>\n                <td class="p-2">0 days</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">diet_restrictions</td>\n                <td class="p-2">Halal</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">support_network</td>\n                <td class="p-2">Family (parents, siblings, children)</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">Question</td>\n                <td class="p-2">I don&#x27;t have a gym—what can I do at home or with everyday items to stay active?</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">generated_queries</td>\n                <td class="p-2">[\n  &quot;What are some effective exercise routines suitable for young female traders with diabetes type 2 living in urban Kano, Nigeria?&quot;,\n  &quot;Are there walking groups or fitness programs for women near my area in Kano tailored for Muslims who observe kosher dietary restrictions?&quot;,\n  &quot;How can Hausa cultural and religious practices in Kano influence my options for daily physical activity as a working adult woman?&quot;,\n  &quot;Where can I find healthy, affordable food options for diabetics in Kano city markets that also comply with kosher guidelines?&quot;,\n  &quot;Is it safe to walk alone for exercise in urban Kano as an 18-24-year-old woman, and are there preferred safe walking routes?&quot;,\n  &quot;How can my daily Qurâ€™an recitation and Islamic studies be combined with gentle physical movements to support my diabetes management?&quot;,\n  &quot;Are there local healthcare professionals or diabetes support groups in Kano that focus on female Muslim patients&#x27; unique needs?&quot;,\n  &quot;What specific challenges do female traders in urban northern Nigeria face in maintaining regular exercise, and how can I overcome them?&quot;,\n  &quot;How can I balance my busy work schedule as a trader in Kano and my need for daily physical activity to help manage my diabetes?&quot;,\n  &quot;Are there traditional Hausa or Islamic approaches in Kano for diabetes management that can complement my current medications?&quot;,\n  &quot;What resources exist in Kano for smokers with diabetes aiming to quit, especially support programs that consider religious and cultural values?&quot;,\n  &quot;Which indoor exercises are most popular or feasible for young Muslim women in Kano who might not have much time or private space at home?&quot;\n]</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">Category</td>\n                <td class="p-2">exercise</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">study_number</td>\n                <td class="p-2">6e73dc05-4f34-4d8e-97b3-94f7e8cf20d0</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">health_goals</td>\n                <td class="p-2">I don&#x27;t have a gym—what can I do at home or with everyday items to stay active?</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">output_format</td>\n                <td class="p-2">Text, Image and audio</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">type</td>\n                <td class="p-2">independent</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">parent</td>\n                <td class="p-2"></td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">label</td>\n                <td class="p-2">BAD</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">story_arc</td>\n                <td class="p-2">classic_change</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">output_tone</td>\n                <td class="p-2">classic_change</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n                </tbody>\n            </table>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n     \n    <style>\n            .guideline-html-content h1 {\n                font-size: 1.1rem;\n                font-weight: 800;\n                margin-bottom: 0.5rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h2 {\n                font-size: 1rem;\n                font-weight: 700;\n                margin-bottom: 0.4rem;\n                margin-top: 1rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h3 {\n                font-size: 0.9rem;\n                font-weight: 600;\n                margin-bottom: 0.3rem;\n                margin-top: 0.8rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content p {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content ul,\n            .guideline-html-content ol {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n                padding-left: 1.25rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content li {\n                margin-bottom: 0.2rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content strong {\n                font-weight: 700;\n                color: #1e293b;\n            }\n        </style> </div> 	Every morning I wake up and prepare breakfast with my children around me, filling our table with tuwo shinkafa and miyan taushe. Do you know, sometimes my day just begins with sitting at my desk for hours, reading Islamic books, or doing reports for my work? That morning, I had to organise the store room—a small task, I thought, but just moving two boxes made me sweat and feel tired quickly. I even forgot to check my blood sugar before starting, because I was thinking only about finishing quickly. Is it not strange how I did not see the link between how my body feels and the work I have to do?\n\nMy mother, who went to the clinic regularly, noticed me pressing my lower back and called Nurse Zainab to visit us. She came in her blue hijab, carrying her gentle smile. Nurse Zainab sat with me on the mat and listened as I told her I don’t have a gym at home and didn’t know how to exercise. She said, 'Fatima, you can start with small things. Climb the stairs two or three times after Fajr prayer. Use water bottles as weights while reading or doing chores. Even walking inside your house to greet each child counts. Simple movement is good for your heart and your sugar.' I looked at her, not sure it would make much difference, but I said, 'I will try, insha’Allah.'\n\nThe next morning, I remembered Nurse Zainab’s advice and carried two one-litre bottles while sweeping my room. I tried climbing the stairs extra slow after each prayer. But, ah, my arms ached and I nearly forgot my midday insulin! For a moment, I thought to stop and return to my old way. But a big task was coming: I must help organise a women’s meeting in our local community centre. That gave me strength and I said, 'Let me continue, maybe I will feel stronger by then.'\n\nDay by day, I started feeling better. My breathing was not so heavy after sweeping. I could carry more groceries without stopping. Finally, the day came for the community meeting. I moved around the room, setting chairs, guiding my friends, and welcoming elders without feeling tired too quickly. How proud I was, and my children saw me smiling as I finished. Now I understand—even small exercise at home really helps. Now, I want to learn more ways to care for my health, because I know it gives me the energy for every duty.	{https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/6e73dc05-4f34-4d8e-97b3-94f7e8cf20d0_0.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/6e73dc05-4f34-4d8e-97b3-94f7e8cf20d0_1.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/6e73dc05-4f34-4d8e-97b3-94f7e8cf20d0_2.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/6e73dc05-4f34-4d8e-97b3-94f7e8cf20d0_3.png}	{https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/6e73dc05-4f34-4d8e-97b3-94f7e8cf20d0_0.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/6e73dc05-4f34-4d8e-97b3-94f7e8cf20d0_1.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/6e73dc05-4f34-4d8e-97b3-94f7e8cf20d0_2.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/6e73dc05-4f34-4d8e-97b3-94f7e8cf20d0_3.mp3}	I don't have a gym—what can I do at home or with everyday items to stay active?	exercise	female	independent	2026-02-22 22:58:58.724409+00	\N
