="p-2">social_support</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">output_tone</td>\n                <td class="p-2">social_support</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n                </tbody>\n            </table>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n     \n    <style>\n            .guideline-html-content h1 {\n                font-size: 1.1rem;\n                font-weight: 800;\n                margin-bottom: 0.5rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h2 {\n                font-size: 1rem;\n                font-weight: 700;\n                margin-bottom: 0.4rem;\n                margin-top: 1rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h3 {\n                font-size: 0.9rem;\n                font-weight: 600;\n                margin-bottom: 0.3rem;\n                margin-top: 0.8rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content p {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content ul,\n            .guideline-html-content ol {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n                padding-left: 1.25rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content li {\n                margin-bottom: 0.2rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content strong {\n                font-weight: 700;\n                color: #1e293b;\n            }\n        </style> </div> 	Let me tell you what happened one ordinary morning on the street side near Sabon Gari. I woke up as usual, rushed my prayers, and quickly ate some leftover tuwo before dashing out with my trading bag. Kai, does a healthy breakfast really matter, I wondered? As soon as I reached the market, we offloaded a fresh pile of onions. I bent to lift a sack, but my arms went weak and my legs shaky. The other boys looked at me as I tried to hide my tiredness. I blamed the dusty air, but deep down I thought, "Is it not just small onions?" My mind drifted to last night at the tea spot, where I skipped my medicine and ate late again.\n\nIn the afternoon, after nearly dozing during a long price haggling, I decided to walk across the road to the clinic nearby. The nurse, Aunty Rahila—a real no-nonsense person—looked at me. She said, 'Kamalu, with your diabetes, you must exercise small-small but not too hard. Why don't you walk daily with your friends before evening tea and choose healthy meals?' I frowned, not too convinced. Can ordinary walking and eating miyan kuka or plenty of vegetables with grilled fish help my energy? She smiled, handed me a leaflet, and reminded me, 'Make sure you time your insulin only with proper meals and do exercise at the same time every day.'\n\nAfter clinic, I tried to change my routine. The next morning, instead of rushing, I joined my friend Musa and we walked around the edge of the Sabon Gari park before work—just slow steps, nothing hard. The first day, I felt awkward and tired; even forgot my snack and nearly argued at work again. It was not easy leaving my comfort, but the memory of yesterday’s weakness followed me. Why give up now, when next week there will be a big rice delivery job? I needed my strength to show I am still the fastest amongst my trader friends.\n\nDay by day, the short walks got easier. I began eating my miyan kuka early, snacks from fruits and peanuts, and timing my insulin, just as the nurse advised. When the big rice delivery came, I was alert, not tired, and lifted every bag myself, smiling. Musa clapped me on the back and said, 'Kamalu, this your new energy, is it not magic?' I just laughed, happy inside. Now, I believe that even small healthy choices can give us the strength for big things, and I already look forward to more walks with my friends after market.	{https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/fd864f85-786d-4ac3-9702-53483798b5d8_0.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/fd864f85-786d-4ac3-9702-53483798b5d8_1.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/fd864f85-786d-4ac3-9702-53483798b5d8_2.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/fd864f85-786d-4ac3-9702-53483798b5d8_3.png}	{https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/fd864f85-786d-4ac3-9702-53483798b5d8_0.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/fd864f85-786d-4ac3-9702-53483798b5d8_1.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/fd864f85-786d-4ac3-9702-53483798b5d8_2.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/fd864f85-786d-4ac3-9702-53483798b5d8_3.mp3}	What kinds of exercises are safe and helpful for someone with diabetes?	exercise	male	overlapped	2026-02-22 22:58:58.834414+00	\N
