  &quot;What is the role of close friend support networks in Hausa culture for managing chronic conditions like diabetes?&quot;,\n  &quot;Are there Hausa-language resources or support groups in Kano specifically for young men with Type 2 diabetes?&quot;,\n  &quot;How do Islamic practices in Kano intersect with diabetes management, especially during fasting periods for someone on insulin or metformin?&quot;,\n  &quot;What are the most popular recreational activities among young, male, working adults in suburban Kano for maintaining physical health?&quot;\n]</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">Category</td>\n                <td class="p-2">diet</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">study_number</td>\n                <td class="p-2">0db70a04-c83a-48ec-8dd9-393ecdbc02b2</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">health_goals</td>\n                <td class="p-2">I sometimes eat late at night. How does this affect my blood sugar, and what can I do instead? </td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">output_format</td>\n                <td class="p-2">Text, Image and audio</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">type</td>\n                <td class="p-2">control</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">parent</td>\n                <td class="p-2"></td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">label</td>\n                <td class="p-2">EXCELLENT</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">story_arc</td>\n                <td class="p-2">social_support</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">output_tone</td>\n                <td class="p-2">social_support</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n                </tbody>\n            </table>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n     \n    <style>\n            .guideline-html-content h1 {\n                font-size: 1.1rem;\n                font-weight: 800;\n                margin-bottom: 0.5rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h2 {\n                font-size: 1rem;\n                font-weight: 700;\n                margin-bottom: 0.4rem;\n                margin-top: 1rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h3 {\n                font-size: 0.9rem;\n                font-weight: 600;\n                margin-bottom: 0.3rem;\n                margin-top: 0.8rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content p {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content ul,\n            .guideline-html-content ol {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n                padding-left: 1.25rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content li {\n                margin-bottom: 0.2rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content strong {\n                font-weight: 700;\n                color: #1e293b;\n            }\n        </style> </div> 	Every day, I get up early, pray, and take my morning insulin, thinking my day will go alright so long as I just follow my normal routine. At work, I often stay late at my desk to finish some project files for the director. After dark, I reach home hungry and usually eat my tuwo with hot vegetable soup, sometimes even close to midnight. I never think much about how late meals might affect anything. One evening, after gulping down a big plate of moin moin late at night, I had to put together a report summary for the new project. My mind felt slow, my eyes heavy, and my hands shaky. The short task that should be easy took me too long. I finished it, but I knew something wasn’t right. Can late-night food really make work more difficult for me?\n\nThe next week at the clinic, Nurse Amina asked, 'Chinonso, have you been monitoring your blood sugar after late dinners?' I shook my head, not sure if it really mattered. She smiled, not scolding, just patient. She explained, 'Eating late, especially heavy food, can keep your sugar high all night. You might wake up tired and struggle at work. Why not try eating your main meal earlier—by 8 pm? If you’re still hungry at night, take a small snack, maybe steamed unripe plantain or veggies, not tuwo with soup. And check your sugar before bed.' I nodded, feeling a little confused but willing to try. After all, Nurse Amina always knows what she’s talking about, and her advice is easy to follow.\n\nThat night, I tried eating at half past seven and skipped my second helping. My friends invited me out, and I almost forgot Nurse Amina’s words! My stomach grumbled when I saw them buying suya and soft drinks. I hesitated—should I join, just a little? But I remembered my report was still waiting for me at home. The habit was hard to break. I nearly gave in, but instead, I made do with roasted groundnuts and plenty of water. My body felt restless for something heavy, and my mind kept thinking, 'Will I manage to focus better?' I was worried about the big training session I had to organize next week for the whole team.\n\nLittle by little, it started paying off. Waking up the next morning, my head was clear, and my body felt lighter. I finished my work summary so quickly and with such confidence, my boss actually smiled and mentioned my improvement. On the day of the bigger training task, I stood in front of the whole department, explaining the new project with energy I hadn’t felt in a while. In the end, I thought, maybe taking small steps with my eating habits does work after all. Now, when my friends ask about my late-night eating, I tell them it's trying new things that keeps life interesting—and my health on track!	{https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/0db70a04-c83a-48ec-8dd9-393ecdbc02b2_0.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/0db70a04-c83a-48ec-8dd9-393ecdbc02b2_1.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/0db70a04-c83a-48ec-8dd9-393ecdbc02b2_2.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/0db70a04-c83a-48ec-8dd9-393ecdbc02b2_3.png}	{https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/0db70a04-c83a-48ec-8dd9-393ecdbc02b2_0.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/0db70a04-c83a-48ec-8dd9-393ecdbc02b2_1.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/0db70a04-c83a-48ec-8dd9-393ecdbc02b2_2.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/0db70a04-c83a-48ec-8dd9-393ecdbc02b2_3.mp3}	I sometimes eat late at night. How does this affect my blood sugar, and what can I do instead? 	diet	male	control	2026-02-22 22:58:59.197593+00	\N
