est markets or shops in urban Katsina for affordable diabetes-friendly groceries for traders with busy work routines?&quot;,\n  &quot;Are there local Hausa herbal or traditional remedies in Katsina commonly used by young women for managing type 2 diabetes alongside prescribed medications?&quot;,\n  &quot;What physical activities are most popular among urban Hausa women in Katsina who exercise 5-7 days a week for diabetes control?&quot;,\n  &quot;How do other young women in Katsina with type 2 diabetes manage regular healthcare visits around their trading schedules?&quot;,\n  &quot;What are the cultural perceptions or stigmas about diabetes among Hausa communities in Katsina, especially for young Christian women?&quot;\n]</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">Category</td>\n                <td class="p-2">diet</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">study_number</td>\n                <td class="p-2">bb875cc5-32e4-4d91-9720-966053c388ff</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">health_goals</td>\n                <td class="p-2">Which everyday foods can I eat that won&#x27;t make my blood sugar spike?</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">output_format</td>\n                <td class="p-2">Text, Image and audio</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">type</td>\n                <td class="p-2">independent</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">parent</td>\n                <td class="p-2"></td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">label</td>\n                <td class="p-2">GOOD</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">story_arc</td>\n                <td class="p-2">default</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">output_tone</td>\n                <td class="p-2">default</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n                </tbody>\n            </table>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n     \n    <style>\n            .guideline-html-content h1 {\n                font-size: 1.1rem;\n                font-weight: 800;\n                margin-bottom: 0.5rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h2 {\n                font-size: 1rem;\n                font-weight: 700;\n                margin-bottom: 0.4rem;\n                margin-top: 1rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h3 {\n                font-size: 0.9rem;\n                font-weight: 600;\n                margin-bottom: 0.3rem;\n                margin-top: 0.8rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content p {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content ul,\n            .guideline-html-content ol {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n                padding-left: 1.25rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content li {\n                margin-bottom: 0.2rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content strong {\n                font-weight: 700;\n                color: #1e293b;\n            }\n        </style> </div> 	One morning, I woke up feeling a bit heavy, but I rushed to the market because I needed to sort out my stock. There were yams and tuwo, lots of fried snacks calling my name, and I gobbled them down with ginger tea. Suddenly, I felt dizzy. Imagine that—right at my own stall, in front of my customers! Because I didn’t think about how food can affect my health, I ended up mixing up customer orders. I was left embarrassed and worried, asking, ‘Why is this happening to me on a busy day?’\n\nLater that afternoon, I met Nurse Grace at the local clinic. She sat close by and listened carefully. At first, I felt shy and wondered if she truly understood how life is for us in Katsina. But Nurse Grace said, ‘Chimamanda, you can eat what everyone eats, just pick foods like beans, okra soup, moi moi, and grilled chicken, not fried puff puff or lots of white bread. Take small portions, drink water, and remember, gluten-free doesn’t mean tasteless!’ She even suggested healthy swaps for our local meals. I nodded, still a bit unsure, but her words sounded simple and wise.\n\nThe next day, I tried the advice. I passed by the fried snacks, even though it was tempting, and chose beans with grilled plantain. My friends laughed and asked, ‘Chimamanda, are you on a diet now?’ I felt out of place. At home, I forgot and almost ate a bowl of pounded yam, but I remembered my health talk and stopped myself. Changing old habits is hard, but I knew I had a big church event coming soon, and I wanted to be strong enough to help with the Sunday decorations.\n\nOver the next weeks, I got used to eating more beans, fresh vegetables, even drinking lemon water. Work in the market became easier—I was less tired and more focused. The big Sunday decoration at church went smoothly, and everyone thanked me for my help. I felt so proud! Now, when I tell stories at gatherings, I talk about how easy changes can make a big difference. Maybe this is just the beginning for me to feel better every day.	{https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/bb875cc5-32e4-4d91-9720-966053c388ff_0.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/bb875cc5-32e4-4d91-9720-966053c388ff_1.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/bb875cc5-32e4-4d91-9720-966053c388ff_2.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/bb875cc5-32e4-4d91-9720-966053c388ff_3.png}	{https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/bb875cc5-32e4-4d91-9720-966053c388ff_0.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/bb875cc5-32e4-4d91-9720-966053c388ff_1.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/bb875cc5-32e4-4d91-9720-966053c388ff_2.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/bb875cc5-32e4-4d91-9720-966053c388ff_3.mp3}	Which everyday foods can I eat that won't make my blood sugar spike?	diet	female	independent	2026-02-22 22:58:59.940856+00	\N
