in Kano city that focus on nutrition and lifestyle management?&quot;,\n  &quot;How can I modify popular Hausa foods like tuwo shinkafa or miyan kuka to be diabetes-friendly while keeping the traditional flavors?&quot;,\n  &quot;What healthy meal options are available near the textile markets in Kano that won&#x27;t affect my blood sugar but are filling for a working adult?&quot;,\n  &quot;Which storytelling or socializing events in Kano are inclusive of women with health conditions like diabetes, and do they offer healthy snacks or meals?&quot;,\n  &quot;Is there a cultural preference for herbal or traditional medicines among Hausa women in Kano with PCOS and diabetes, and what does local research say about its effectiveness?&quot;,\n  &quot;Where can I find dieticians or diabetes educators in Kano experienced with Hausa cuisine and Islamic practices who help women like me manage blood sugar and PCOS?&quot;\n]</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">Category</td>\n                <td class="p-2">exercise</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">study_number</td>\n                <td class="p-2">afc17e7b-12ec-4e0a-ab8f-84d6b8ff59fb</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">health_goals</td>\n                <td class="p-2">I don&#x27;t have a gym—what can I do at home or with everyday items to stay active?</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">output_format</td>\n                <td class="p-2">Text, Image and audio</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">type</td>\n                <td class="p-2">consistency</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">parent</td>\n                <td class="p-2">ae7a7371-62cc-4f01-964a-2649369db9b0</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">label</td>\n                <td class="p-2">EXCELLENT</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">story_arc</td>\n                <td class="p-2">social_support</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">output_tone</td>\n                <td class="p-2">social_support</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n                </tbody>\n            </table>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n     \n    <style>\n            .guideline-html-content h1 {\n                font-size: 1.1rem;\n                font-weight: 800;\n                margin-bottom: 0.5rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h2 {\n                font-size: 1rem;\n                font-weight: 700;\n                margin-bottom: 0.4rem;\n                margin-top: 1rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h3 {\n                font-size: 0.9rem;\n                font-weight: 600;\n                margin-bottom: 0.3rem;\n                margin-top: 0.8rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content p {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content ul,\n            .guideline-html-content ol {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n                padding-left: 1.25rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content li {\n                margin-bottom: 0.2rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content strong {\n                font-weight: 700;\n                color: #1e293b;\n            }\n        </style> </div> 	Let me tell you about my Tuesday last week. I stood early, as usual, rising before Fajr prayer. In my house in busy Kano, I cooked millet tuwo quickly and packed kuli-kuli and suya for lunch. Isn’t it sometimes easier to ignore all those talks about ‘healthy’ exercise, especially when the market never waits? I walked to my shop near Sabon Gari and started arranging textiles. By noon, my legs were heavy and I felt dizzy. Ah, how can one focus on customers if the body is not cooperating? I tried to help a buyer with a big bale of fabric, but my energy dropped sharply—I had to sit down. Someone else carried the load for me. That’s how I missed a promising sale, all because I didn't think much about managing my daily activity and my meals.\n\nLater that day, when I went for my regular check at the local clinic, the nurse saw I looked tired. She asked about my day and health. I almost shrugged, but you know, she is kind and patient. She said, 'Chinelo, you don’t need a gym to stay strong or manage your blood sugar. Walk briskly around your shop in the morning, do gentle squats behind your stall when business is slow, and stretch your legs every hour. Use water bottles at home to do easy arm exercises before Maghrib. And always eat a small snack, like roasted groundnuts or moi-moi, before tough tasks, so your sugar won’t drop suddenly.' I nodded, still unsure, wondering if these small things could really help such a busy person as me.\n\nThe next morning at home, I set two water bottles on the floor and started stretching. I felt awkward, thinking, 'Is this really exercise?' Still, I bent my knees, lifted the bottles, and walked briskly from my sitting room to the kitchen and back. At the market, I tried squatting by my bench during slow moments, but one customer laughed—she thought I dropped something! I almost stopped, but then I remembered tomorrow’s textile delivery: a heavy load I would need to move myself if my worker didn't show up. I shook off the embarrassment and stretched again, determined not to give up just because of a small setback like feeling clumsy.\n\nBy the end of the week, something had changed. I packed a small bowl of bean porridge, remembered my stretches every morning, and moved more during work. Saturday came—the delivery day. As I lifted the big bale off the cart, my arms were steadier, and my legs no longer felt weak. Could it be that small exercises made this difference? I even had breath to greet my colleagues cheerfully! That success made me believe: if simple moves and healthy snacks could help with one big task, maybe I could become even stronger. Now, I look forward to building my own routine, little by little, and maybe inspire my friends in Kano market too.	{https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/afc17e7b-12ec-4e0a-ab8f-84d6b8ff59fb_0.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/afc17e7b-12ec-4e0a-ab8f-84d6b8ff59fb_1.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/afc17e7b-12ec-4e0a-ab8f-84d6b8ff59fb_2.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/afc17e7b-12ec-4e0a-ab8f-84d6b8ff59fb_3.png}	{https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/afc17e7b-12ec-4e0a-ab8f-84d6b8ff59fb_0.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/afc17e7b-12ec-4e0a-ab8f-84d6b8ff59fb_1.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/afc17e7b-12ec-4e0a-ab8f-84d6b8ff59fb_2.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/afc17e7b-12ec-4e0a-ab8f-84d6b8ff59fb_3.mp3}	I don't have a gym—what can I do at home or with everyday items to stay active?	exercise	female	consistency	2026-02-22 22:59:00.318385+00	\N
