ption interact with medications like insulin and Metformin for young adults in Nigeria?&quot;,\n  &quot;What services do local healthcare clinics in Kano offer specifically for student diabetes management and education?&quot;,\n  &quot;How can family members in Hausa culture support a young male relative managing type 2 diabetes while studying in an urban area?&quot;,\n  &quot;Are there exercise facilities or safe outdoor areas in Kano that accommodate young adults with diabetes&#x27; needs?&quot;\n]</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">Category</td>\n                <td class="p-2">diet</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">study_number</td>\n                <td class="p-2">8905e068-2973-4a40-82a5-b011e7e64822</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">health_goals</td>\n                <td class="p-2">I like to snack—what are some healthy options and how often should I have them?</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">output_format</td>\n                <td class="p-2">Text, Image and audio</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">type</td>\n                <td class="p-2">overlapped</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">parent</td>\n                <td class="p-2"></td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">label</td>\n                <td class="p-2">EXCELLENT</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">story_arc</td>\n                <td class="p-2">social_support</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">output_tone</td>\n                <td class="p-2">social_support</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n                </tbody>\n            </table>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n     \n    <style>\n            .guideline-html-content h1 {\n                font-size: 1.1rem;\n                font-weight: 800;\n                margin-bottom: 0.5rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h2 {\n                font-size: 1rem;\n                font-weight: 700;\n                margin-bottom: 0.4rem;\n                margin-top: 1rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h3 {\n                font-size: 0.9rem;\n                font-weight: 600;\n                margin-bottom: 0.3rem;\n                margin-top: 0.8rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content p {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content ul,\n            .guideline-html-content ol {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n                padding-left: 1.25rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content li {\n                margin-bottom: 0.2rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content strong {\n                font-weight: 700;\n                color: #1e293b;\n            }\n        </style> </div> 	Some days, I think, "Is it even a big deal to grab puff-puff and zobo on the way to class?" This morning was like every other – rushing, backpack slung over one shoulder, munching pastries while scrolling my phone. Who has time for healthy snacking when life is this busy? Later, during a study group, I felt dizzy, my hands shaking a bit. My notes looked blurry, and my mates asked if I was fasting. I laughed it off, blaming late breakfast. At the library, I tried to focus on an assignment about Kano Pillars football history—but everything felt slow and hard. I just wanted to finish quickly, but I couldn't. Did I mess up because of something simple like the snacks I ate?\n\nWhen I stopped by the campus clinic, Nurse Halima saw me looking confused and tired. She didn’t scold, you know. Instead, she smiled, saying, "Manu, snacks are not the enemy. It is how and what you snack that matters. Next time, try packing small portions of groundnuts, garden eggs, or moi moi in your bag. Dan Wake or roasted corn is good too—easy to find near campus and keeps sugar steady. Have them once between breakfast and lunch, then again before football practice so you don’t go low. Always check your sugar if you feel odd. You see, staying ready is part of being a champion on and off the pitch, wallahi." It sounded simple, but could snack choices change everything?\n\nI tried that advice the next day. Honestly, it was not easy changing what I buy from the market after school. I almost took my old snacks, but I remembered the nurse’s words and picked boiled groundnuts instead—just enough for a small bag. During group work, my friends laughed at my new snack. In the evening, before heading to football at Milkyway Academy, I had garden eggs and water. It felt strange, but hey, I was getting ready for trials at the big local club next week—if I messed up now, my chance could pass me by. Bad habits are hard to break, but I stayed stubborn, focusing on the goal.\n\nOver time, I got used to these changes. My bag always has a small pack of healthy snacks now—sometimes suya sticks without too much oil. I noticed my energy stays better, and no more shakes during classes. The football trial came, and I felt strong—no dizziness, no drama. I scored two goals and made new friends. Now, I even help my siblings choose snacks after mosque and tell them, 'Little changes, big difference.' You see, managing snacks is not just about food, it’s about winning in life. I am ready for more challenges, healthier and hopeful!	{https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/8905e068-2973-4a40-82a5-b011e7e64822_0.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/8905e068-2973-4a40-82a5-b011e7e64822_1.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/8905e068-2973-4a40-82a5-b011e7e64822_2.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/8905e068-2973-4a40-82a5-b011e7e64822_3.png}	{https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/8905e068-2973-4a40-82a5-b011e7e64822_0.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/8905e068-2973-4a40-82a5-b011e7e64822_1.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/8905e068-2973-4a40-82a5-b011e7e64822_2.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/8905e068-2973-4a40-82a5-b011e7e64822_3.mp3}	I like to snack—what are some healthy options and how often should I have them?	diet	male	overlapped	2026-02-22 22:58:58.959263+00	\N
