e and diabetes?&quot;,\n  &quot;Are there educational diabetes support groups at clinics or hospitals in Kano that cater to Hausa-speaking adults with type 2 diabetes?&quot;,\n  &quot;What are seasonal trends in fresh produce availability near Kano, and how can I plan a diabetes-friendly, lactose-free diet around them?&quot;,\n  &quot;How do other working adults in Kano manage fatigue and maintain motivation for diabetes care with family and social responsibilities?&quot;,\n  &quot;What farming-related physical activities can help improve blood sugar control for a man in his late 30s or early 40s living in suburban Kano?&quot;,\n  &quot;How does access to suburban healthcare facilities in Kano impact diabetes outcomes compared to patients living in rural or urban areas?&quot;\n]</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">Category</td>\n                <td class="p-2">diet</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">study_number</td>\n                <td class="p-2">152a388d-e444-4f4a-9d9c-302193f19eec</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">health_goals</td>\n                <td class="p-2">I like to snack—what are some healthy options and how often should I have them?</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">output_format</td>\n                <td class="p-2">Text, Image and audio</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">type</td>\n                <td class="p-2">overlapped</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">parent</td>\n                <td class="p-2"></td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">label</td>\n                <td class="p-2">EXCELLENT</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">story_arc</td>\n                <td class="p-2">social_support</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">output_tone</td>\n                <td class="p-2">social_support</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n                </tbody>\n            </table>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n     \n    <style>\n            .guideline-html-content h1 {\n                font-size: 1.1rem;\n                font-weight: 800;\n                margin-bottom: 0.5rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h2 {\n                font-size: 1rem;\n                font-weight: 700;\n                margin-bottom: 0.4rem;\n                margin-top: 1rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h3 {\n                font-size: 0.9rem;\n                font-weight: 600;\n                margin-bottom: 0.3rem;\n                margin-top: 0.8rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content p {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content ul,\n            .guideline-html-content ol {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n                padding-left: 1.25rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content li {\n                margin-bottom: 0.2rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content strong {\n                font-weight: 700;\n                color: #1e293b;\n            }\n        </style> </div> 	One day at the market, I was helping my friend arrange bags of onions for customers. I hadn’t eaten since early morning and saw some sweet buns, so I grabbed two and ate them quickly. Eh, why should I worry? I thought, it’s just small food. But before noon, I started feeling dizzy and so tired I couldn’t finish arranging the next sack. Even with easy access to good food, sometimes I just eat what is in front of me. Small mistake, but it made everything hard that day.\n\nLater, the health worker from the local clinic passed by. She noticed I looked sweaty and sat me down under a tree. "Baba Mutari," she said, "you need a different kind of snack, not sweet buns. Try roasted groundnuts, kuli kuli, or small pieces of boiled corn, and don’t eat big portions all at once. Carry a tin in your pocket. For someone with diabetes, snacking means eating healthy, not just eating by the clock." I wanted to argue—this is not how I grew up—but her gentle voice made sense. Maybe that’s what I need.\n\nSo, I followed her advice the next day. I packed kuli kuli and groundnuts from home, but honestly, I almost forgot and bought suya instead. It’s hard to change. At first, I wanted to complain, but I remembered I must help offload a new truck of goods soon, a bigger task than yesterday. That thought kept me steady. Eating the groundnuts slowly, I felt a little better by afternoon, though it took practice not to run back to the sweet buns.\n\nOver time, it got easier. By the week’s end, I managed the big delivery without feeling faint once. Farmers who came to buy from the market noticed I had energy. I was proud. Now, I carry healthy snacks and feel more ready to keep learning. Isn’t it funny how one small change makes everything possible? Now, I always ask myself: what healthy thing can I pick today?	{https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/152a388d-e444-4f4a-9d9c-302193f19eec_0.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/152a388d-e444-4f4a-9d9c-302193f19eec_1.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/152a388d-e444-4f4a-9d9c-302193f19eec_2.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/152a388d-e444-4f4a-9d9c-302193f19eec_3.png}	{https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/152a388d-e444-4f4a-9d9c-302193f19eec_0.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/152a388d-e444-4f4a-9d9c-302193f19eec_1.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/152a388d-e444-4f4a-9d9c-302193f19eec_2.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/152a388d-e444-4f4a-9d9c-302193f19eec_3.mp3}	I like to snack—what are some healthy options and how often should I have them?	diet	male	overlapped	2026-02-22 22:58:59.318053+00	\N
