y used in Kano interact with insulin or metformin for type 2 diabetes?&quot;,\n  &quot;Where can I find urban football teams or leagues in Kano suitable for adults with limited support networks seeking exercise?&quot;,\n  &quot;What are the most common challenges for young male traders in Kano with type 2 diabetes, and how can they overcome limited social support?&quot;,\n  &quot;Are there Hausa-language resources or educational materials about managing anxiety and diabetes in northern Nigerian cities?&quot;,\n  &quot;What steps should a Muslim in Kano take to reduce high alcohol consumption considering its impact on type 2 diabetes and mental health?&quot;\n]</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">Category</td>\n                <td class="p-2">diet</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">study_number</td>\n                <td class="p-2">277fc7a1-6997-4d85-a7d8-139f5f503879</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">health_goals</td>\n                <td class="p-2">I sometimes eat late at night. How does this affect my blood sugar, and what can I do instead? </td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">output_format</td>\n                <td class="p-2">Text, Image and audio</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">type</td>\n                <td class="p-2">independent</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">parent</td>\n                <td class="p-2"></td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">label</td>\n                <td class="p-2">EXCELLENT</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">story_arc</td>\n                <td class="p-2">resistance</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">output_tone</td>\n                <td class="p-2">resistance</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n                </tbody>\n            </table>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n     \n    <style>\n            .guideline-html-content h1 {\n                font-size: 1.1rem;\n                font-weight: 800;\n                margin-bottom: 0.5rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h2 {\n                font-size: 1rem;\n                font-weight: 700;\n                margin-bottom: 0.4rem;\n                margin-top: 1rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h3 {\n                font-size: 0.9rem;\n                font-weight: 600;\n                margin-bottom: 0.3rem;\n                margin-top: 0.8rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content p {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content ul,\n            .guideline-html-content ol {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n                padding-left: 1.25rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content li {\n                margin-bottom: 0.2rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content strong {\n                font-weight: 700;\n                color: #1e293b;\n            }\n        </style> </div> 	Every morning, I wake up in my small flat in Sabon Gari, right before the mosque call ends, and get myself ready for the busy market. Sometimes, I skip breakfast if I feel tired, and when work drags on till late, I end up eating at 11 or even midnight. You know how it is—food is easy to find on our street, from gwate to small tuwo, and even fried kosai, but who really thinks about sugar at that time? Last time, I wanted to set up my stall for the new school bag delivery, but halfway—my body just felt weak, and my mind seemed cloudy. I couldn't finish sorting the bags before maghrib, and buyers just passed by. Was it the late food? Or was I just tired?\n\nA few days later, at the local clinic near Sabon Gari roundabout, Sister Maryam, the nurse, listened to my grumbling. I told her about always feeling weak after eating late. She didn’t shout or make me feel useless. 'Tariq, late-night eating can make your sugar rise and fall the wrong way,' she said in simple English, 'If you try to eat lighter—like moi moi, or fish stew with vegetables—before sunset, and just have water or tea before bed, you’ll feel better in the morning and think clearer at work.' She advised, 'Playing football or walking 30 minutes before going home helps too.' I sat there nodding, but inside I wondered, can simple changes really work for me?\n\nI decided to try it. On Monday, I turned down suya at 10pm, forcing myself to eat early. But you know, changing old habits is not easy. That night, I was awake late, busy with WhatsApp, feeling the hunger in my stomach. I almost gave in! But the big school bag consignment was coming soon, and I told myself, if I feel better with these small changes, maybe I can sell more and not disappoint the market supervisor again. I drank tea, tried to rest, and planned to walk to the shop in the morning.\n\nIt wasn’t magic, but after one week, things started changing. I felt more energy in the morning, walked briskly to the shop, and my hands didn’t shake during sales. When the big consignment finally arrived, I arranged the bags with a steady hand and a clear head, even chatting and joking with the other traders. Customers noticed my bright mood, and I sold out my section in one day. Now, I’m thinking, what if I make these habits regular? I’m not perfect yet, but I can see for myself—small changes make bigger wins.	{https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/277fc7a1-6997-4d85-a7d8-139f5f503879_0.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/277fc7a1-6997-4d85-a7d8-139f5f503879_1.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/277fc7a1-6997-4d85-a7d8-139f5f503879_2.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/277fc7a1-6997-4d85-a7d8-139f5f503879_3.png}	{https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/277fc7a1-6997-4d85-a7d8-139f5f503879_0.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/277fc7a1-6997-4d85-a7d8-139f5f503879_1.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/277fc7a1-6997-4d85-a7d8-139f5f503879_2.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/277fc7a1-6997-4d85-a7d8-139f5f503879_3.mp3}	I sometimes eat late at night. How does this affect my blood sugar, and what can I do instead? 	diet	male	independent	2026-02-22 22:58:59.671593+00	\N
