re for Hausa men under 35?&quot;,\n  &quot;What are the challenges and solutions for sticking to diabetes medication regimens as an urban trader in Kano with an irregular routine?&quot;,\n  &quot;Is there a connection between late meal times and fasting during Ramadan for Hausa Muslims with diabetes, and how should I adjust my routine?&quot;,\n  &quot;What strategies do other male traders in Kano use to avoid smoking throughout the workday, especially with high daily stress?&quot;,\n  &quot;Are there culturally-accepted herbal or traditional medicines in Hausa culture that are compatible with prescribed diabetes medications?&quot;\n]</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">Category</td>\n                <td class="p-2">diet</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">study_number</td>\n                <td class="p-2">f02c6c0b-2b64-4b38-9c68-7b0e45c2794d</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">health_goals</td>\n                <td class="p-2">Can you give me some simple meal ideas or a sample daily menu I could follow?</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">output_format</td>\n                <td class="p-2">Text, Image and audio</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">type</td>\n                <td class="p-2">overlapped</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">parent</td>\n                <td class="p-2"></td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">label</td>\n                <td class="p-2">EXCELLENT</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">story_arc</td>\n                <td class="p-2">social_support</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">output_tone</td>\n                <td class="p-2">social_support</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n                </tbody>\n            </table>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n     \n    <style>\n            .guideline-html-content h1 {\n                font-size: 1.1rem;\n                font-weight: 800;\n                margin-bottom: 0.5rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h2 {\n                font-size: 1rem;\n                font-weight: 700;\n                margin-bottom: 0.4rem;\n                margin-top: 1rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h3 {\n                font-size: 0.9rem;\n                font-weight: 600;\n                margin-bottom: 0.3rem;\n                margin-top: 0.8rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content p {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content ul,\n            .guideline-html-content ol {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n                padding-left: 1.25rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content li {\n                margin-bottom: 0.2rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content strong {\n                font-weight: 700;\n                color: #1e293b;\n            }\n        </style> </div> 	Every morning, I open my shop in Sabon Gari Market early, hoping for good sales. Most times, for breakfast, I just grab some tuwo or fried bread from a street vendor, then rush off to arrange my wares before the customers land. Sometimes, I feel a bit dizzy but I push on—who has time to worry about what you eat when sales dey call? Last week, I had to deliver goods to a big customer. But wallahi, I started sweating, my hand dey shake, and I couldn’t finish loading the goods. The man vex small and left. Was it because I did not eat enough, or maybe I just too stubborn for food wahala?\n\nThe next day, one nurse from the local clinic, Aunty Hadiza, stopped by the market to ask after us traders. I dey tire to talk about my diabetes again—abeg, which talk dem never give us before? But she just smiled and told me, 'Chinonso, let’s start small. For a trader like you, just pack beans cake—kosai—or roasted groundnut with you in the morning. In the afternoon, try eat some miyan kuka soup with brown rice or danwake. Evening, chop vegetables or moi moi. Skip pastries, and try little portions. You’ll see your strength return and you’ll stop feeling faint.' Her voice was soft but I hear am well. Is it really that simple?\n\nThat night, I packed a small tub of moi moi and some roasted groundnuts for the next day. Habits hard to break; as I reach market, the smell of fried bread tempt me again. I nearly forget my own snack, but then I remember the heavy work ahead. I eat my moi moi and continue sorting my goods, though it felt strange to change my oga-style. Around noon, I almost reached for a sweet kola from the neighbour, but stopped myself—change na wahala oh! Still, the big delivery was coming soon, and I no wan fail again.\n\nBy afternoon, I chop my small prepared meal and felt stronger. This time, I carried my goods with confidence and finished the delivery. The customer noticed, smiled and even promised more business. Me wey be Chinonso, I felt one kind big pride. Maybe small small changes, e fit build up; I begin see that taking care of myself, no be waste of time for this my trade. I even started thinking, could I add more walk to my day or try another vegetables tomorrow? The fear of food wahala fit reduce, if I just dey try and learn new ways.	{https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/f02c6c0b-2b64-4b38-9c68-7b0e45c2794d_0.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/f02c6c0b-2b64-4b38-9c68-7b0e45c2794d_1.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/f02c6c0b-2b64-4b38-9c68-7b0e45c2794d_2.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/f02c6c0b-2b64-4b38-9c68-7b0e45c2794d_3.png}	{https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/f02c6c0b-2b64-4b38-9c68-7b0e45c2794d_0.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/f02c6c0b-2b64-4b38-9c68-7b0e45c2794d_1.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/f02c6c0b-2b64-4b38-9c68-7b0e45c2794d_2.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/f02c6c0b-2b64-4b38-9c68-7b0e45c2794d_3.mp3}	Can you give me some simple meal ideas or a sample daily menu I could follow?	diet	male	overlapped	2026-02-22 22:59:00.091772+00	\N
