and mental health?&quot;,\n  &quot;What are the best local herbal or traditional medicines for managing type 2 diabetes in Kano, and are they safe to use with insulin and oral medications?&quot;,\n  &quot;Are there online or radio Hausa-language fitness resources or instructors who focus on womenâ€™s health and Islamic values in northern Nigeria?&quot;,\n  &quot;How do dietary restrictions like eating kosher (or halal) affect managing diabetes in the Hausa Muslim community of Kano?&quot;,\n  &quot;What anxiety or depression self-care strategies are recommended for young Muslim women in Nigeria, especially those with a busy work life and health concerns like diabetes?&quot;,\n  &quot;During Ramadan, how can I safely adjust my physical activity and medication schedule as a young woman with type 2 diabetes living in suburban Kano?&quot;\n]</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">Category</td>\n                <td class="p-2">diet</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">study_number</td>\n                <td class="p-2">da4a33b5-1d5e-44a0-89c3-5b8ac7caf14d</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">health_goals</td>\n                <td class="p-2">I sometimes eat late at night. How does this affect my blood sugar, and what can I do instead? </td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">output_format</td>\n                <td class="p-2">Text, Image and audio</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">type</td>\n                <td class="p-2">control</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">parent</td>\n                <td class="p-2"></td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">label</td>\n                <td class="p-2">EXCELLENT</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">story_arc</td>\n                <td class="p-2">resistance</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">output_tone</td>\n                <td class="p-2">resistance</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n                </tbody>\n            </table>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n     \n    <style>\n            .guideline-html-content h1 {\n                font-size: 1.1rem;\n                font-weight: 800;\n                margin-bottom: 0.5rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h2 {\n                font-size: 1rem;\n                font-weight: 700;\n                margin-bottom: 0.4rem;\n                margin-top: 1rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h3 {\n                font-size: 0.9rem;\n                font-weight: 600;\n                margin-bottom: 0.3rem;\n                margin-top: 0.8rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content p {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content ul,\n            .guideline-html-content ol {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n                padding-left: 1.25rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content li {\n                margin-bottom: 0.2rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content strong {\n                font-weight: 700;\n                color: #1e293b;\n            }\n        </style> </div> 	One day, my little cousin Hauwa asked for help with her homework, and while I was tired, I said yes. My body felt sluggish and my mind was slow, and, honestly, I snapped at her when she wanted to read aloud. She looked so surprised and I knew I was not being myself. I realised later I ate late—again—and felt this way every time. Still, I thought, does it really matter?\n\nSoon after, the nurse from the local clinic came by for routine health checks and saw how I'm always yawning lately. She sat me down quietly and explained, 'Fatima, when you eat late, especially heavy food before sleeping, your blood sugar can stay high or drop suddenly in the middle of the night. That’s why you’re so tired and irritable. Instead, try eating dinner earlier and if you need a snack at night, take a small serving of grilled chicken or beans, not yam. And, try walking around your compound after Maghrib. Just ten minutes, wallahi, you will see.' I wanted to argue, but she smiled and added, 'Start small, see how you feel.' Simple, but different from my normal style, you know?\n\nChanging my routine was harder than I thought. The first night, I tried to close my shop earlier. My mother teased me, 'Fatima, you’re running from profit!' I wanted to continue as before, but remembered Hauwa’s sad face and the clinic nurse’s calm advice. I ate grilled fish with cabbage salad before Maghrib, walked slowly around my yard, then sat for Qur’an recitation. But honestly, I felt like I wasn’t getting enough energy for my work—what if I can’t handle tomorrow’s big market order? I nearly gave up right there.\n\nBut I stuck to the plan. Each day, walking got easier, and my mind cleared up, slowly. When the big delivery day came, I woke up earlier without heavy tiredness, finished my Islamic study, and managed the order with a lighter heart and sharper mind. Customers even noticed my brighter mood. That’s when I realised: maybe changing my habits is worth it. Maybe I can keep improving, one step at a time.	{https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/da4a33b5-1d5e-44a0-89c3-5b8ac7caf14d_0.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/da4a33b5-1d5e-44a0-89c3-5b8ac7caf14d_1.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/da4a33b5-1d5e-44a0-89c3-5b8ac7caf14d_2.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/da4a33b5-1d5e-44a0-89c3-5b8ac7caf14d_3.png}	{https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/da4a33b5-1d5e-44a0-89c3-5b8ac7caf14d_0.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/da4a33b5-1d5e-44a0-89c3-5b8ac7caf14d_1.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/da4a33b5-1d5e-44a0-89c3-5b8ac7caf14d_2.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/da4a33b5-1d5e-44a0-89c3-5b8ac7caf14d_3.mp3}	I sometimes eat late at night. How does this affect my blood sugar, and what can I do instead? 	diet	female	control	2026-02-22 22:59:00.429496+00	\N
