      </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">alcohol</td>\n                <td class="p-2">No</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">physical_activity</td>\n                <td class="p-2">3-4 days</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">diet_restrictions</td>\n                <td class="p-2">Halal</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">support_network</td>\n                <td class="p-2">Community or religious group</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">Question</td>\n                <td class="p-2">I don&#x27;t have a gym—what can I do at home or with everyday items to stay active?</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">generated_queries</td>\n                <td class="p-2">[\n  &quot;What are some popular urban walking routes in Kiambu suitable for young women with type 2 diabetes?&quot;,\n  &quot;Are there any lactose-free Kikuyu recipes using ingredients easily found in Kiambu&#x27;s urban markets?&quot;,\n  &quot;As a Baptist politician in Kenya, how can I incorporate faith-based community support into my diabetes management?&quot;,\n  &quot;Which crafts activities practiced by Kikuyu women can help increase my physical activity besides walking?&quot;,\n  &quot;What lifestyle changes have helped other young Kenyan women in politics manage type 2 diabetes?&quot;,\n  &quot;What are the best political networking events in Kiambu that also encourage healthy socializing for women with diabetes?&quot;,\n  &quot;Where can I find local diabetes support groups or workshops for young adults in Kiambuâ€™s urban centers?&quot;,\n  &quot;Are there health insurance options in Kenya covering regular diabetes check-ups at local clinics?&quot;,\n  &quot;What types of physical activities are considered safe and effective for 18â€“24-year-old women with type 2 diabetes in urban Kenya?&quot;,\n  &quot;What are the latest diabetes care guidelines at urban healthcare clinics in Kiambu County?&quot;,\n  &quot;How do other young, urban Kikuyu women balance busy political careers with maintaining healthy eating and exercise habits?&quot;,\n  &quot;Are there any community initiatives in Kiambu that promote crafts and health awareness for young adults?&quot;\n]</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">Category</td>\n                <td class="p-2">exercise</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">study_number</td>\n                <td class="p-2">09a52571-b0b2-4e8f-be68-1a579216a386</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">health_goals</td>\n                <td class="p-2">I don&#x27;t have a gym—what can I do at home or with everyday items to stay active?</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">output_format</td>\n                <td class="p-2">Text, Image and audio</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">type</td>\n                <td class="p-2">overlapped</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">parent</td>\n                <td class="p-2"></td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">label</td>\n                <td class="p-2">EXCELLENT</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">story_arc</td>\n                <td class="p-2">social_support</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">output_tone</td>\n                <td class="p-2">social_support</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n                </tbody>\n            </table>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n     \n    <style>\n            .guideline-html-content h1 {\n                font-size: 1.1rem;\n                font-weight: 800;\n                margin-bottom: 0.5rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h2 {\n                font-size: 1rem;\n                font-weight: 700;\n                margin-bottom: 0.4rem;\n                margin-top: 1rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h3 {\n                font-size: 0.9rem;\n                font-weight: 600;\n                margin-bottom: 0.3rem;\n                margin-top: 0.8rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content p {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content ul,\n            .guideline-html-content ol {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n                padding-left: 1.25rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content li {\n                margin-bottom: 0.2rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content strong {\n                font-weight: 700;\n                color: #1e293b;\n            }\n        </style> </div> 	Later, I stopped at our local Kiambu clinic just to pick my supplies. There, Nurse Lucy looked at me and asked, ‘Wanjiku, are you keeping up with being active?’ I laughed and said, ‘Who has time for gym?’ She smiled kindly and explained, ‘You don’t need a gym. Try walking in Karura Forest or even Paradise Lost—safe and beautiful. Or if you want, try simple crafts like basket weaving; gathering and making those baskets keeps you moving! Even dancing to gospel at church or stretching at home counts. Just thirty minutes, three times a week.’ I felt unsure and mumbled, ‘I’m not even sure where to start.’ She nodded, reminding me, ‘Start small, do what you enjoy, and remember to keep it halal and light.’ It sounded possible, but could I really fit that in?\n\nThe next morning I set my mind to try. Before breakfast, I found my scarf and took a slow walk on our street. My legs protested and my body wanted to turn back for chai. I almost did, but I kept thinking—there’s a council women’s leadership forum coming soon, and I can’t afford to feel weak. So, I slowed down, took bigger breaths, and waved at my neighbour. Later, I tried basket weaving in the evening, but my fingers fumbled and my back ached quickly. Isn’t it funny how even small changes feel big? Still, I promised myself I’d try again tomorrow.\n\nAfter a week, it got easier. I even convinced Mama Wambui from church to join me for short walks after evening service, and together we tried dancing to some Kikuyu songs at home. The big forum day arrived, and this time, climbing the stairs at the county office felt easier—I was even smiling and greeting people, not just catching my breath. I realised, if I just keep fitting these small things into my day, looking after my health could become as normal as my morning prayers. With faith and new habits, anything is possible, isn’t it?	{https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/09a52571-b0b2-4e8f-be68-1a579216a386_0.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/09a52571-b0b2-4e8f-be68-1a579216a386_1.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/09a52571-b0b2-4e8f-be68-1a579216a386_2.png}	{https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/09a52571-b0b2-4e8f-be68-1a579216a386_0.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/09a52571-b0b2-4e8f-be68-1a579216a386_1.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/09a52571-b0b2-4e8f-be68-1a579216a386_2.mp3}	I don't have a gym—what can I do at home or with everyday items to stay active?	exercise	female	overlapped	2026-03-01 15:11:10.80939+00	\N
