tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">occupation</td>\n                <td class="p-2">Dairy farmer</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">daily_routine</td>\n                <td class="p-2">Working adult</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">hobbies</td>\n                <td class="p-2">Volleyball</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">activities</td>\n                <td class="p-2">Exercise or physical activities</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">health_conditions</td>\n                <td class="p-2">Polycystic Ovary Syndrome (PCOS)</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">medication</td>\n                <td class="p-2">Insulin injections, Oral medication (e.g., Metformin), Lifestyle changes only (no medication)</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">healthcare_resources</td>\n                <td class="p-2">Local healthcare clinic or hospital</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">healthcare_access</td>\n                <td class="p-2">Yes</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">healthcare_frequency</td>\n                <td class="p-2">Regularly (at least once a year)</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">culture</td>\n                <td class="p-2">Kikuyu</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">t2d_status</td>\n                <td class="p-2">Yes</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">tobacco</td>\n                <td class="p-2">Yes</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">alcohol</td>\n                <td class="p-2">No</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">physical_activity</td>\n                <td class="p-2">3-4 days</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">diet_restrictions</td>\n                <td class="p-2">Halal</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">support_network</td>\n                <td class="p-2">Healthcare provider or counsellor</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">Question</td>\n                <td class="p-2">I sometimes eat late at night. How does this affect my blood sugar, and what can I do instead? </td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">generated_queries</td>\n                <td class="p-2">[\n  &quot;What are some effective home workout routines for young Kikuyu women living in urban Kiambu with PCOS and type 2 diabetes?&quot;,\n  &quot;Which local resources or parks in Kiambu town are suitable for volleyball practice and exercise for women aged 18â€“24?&quot;,\n  &quot;How can a dairy farmer in Kiambu manage PCOS and type 2 diabetes while adhering to a Halal diet and maintaining regular physical activity?&quot;,\n  &quot;What are some quick, no-equipment exercises that fit into a working adult&#x27;s schedule in Kiambu&#x27;s urban areas?&quot;,\n  &quot;Are there any Kikuyu or Zion Christian Church community groups in Kiambu that organize fitness or health-related activities for young women?&quot;,\n  &quot;Which healthy, Halal, dairy-rich recipes are recommended for people in Kenya with both PCOS and diabetes?&quot;,\n  &quot;What is the best way to balance insulin treatments, oral medication, and lifestyle changes for young female dairy farmers with busy routines in Kiambu?&quot;,\n  &quot;How does rare smoking and weekly alcohol consumption affect progress in managing type 2 diabetes and PCOS for young women in Kenya?&quot;,\n  &quot;What affordable at-home exercise equipment is easy to find in Kiambu urban shops for women without access to a gym?&quot;,\n  &quot;Are there any local healthcare clinics in Kiambu offering support specifically for young women with PCOS and diabetes?&quot;,\n  &quot;Can you recommend Kikuyu or Kenyan cultural practices that encourage physical activity and social support for women&#x27;s health?&quot;,\n  &quot;What strategies can help dairy farmers in urban Kenya avoid unhealthy snacking while working and managing dietary restrictions like Halal?&quot;\n]</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">Category</td>\n                <td class="p-2">diet</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">study_number</td>\n                <td class="p-2">c2a50ef7-ddbd-416c-89cf-f9a4ddc766da</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">health_goals</td>\n                <td class="p-2">I sometimes eat late at night. How does this affect my blood sugar, and what can I do instead? </td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">output_format</td>\n                <td class="p-2">Text, Image and audio</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">type</td>\n                <td class="p-2">overlapped</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">parent</td>\n                <td class="p-2"></td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">label</td>\n                <td class="p-2">EXCELLENT</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">story_arc</td>\n                <td class="p-2">social_support</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">output_tone</td>\n                <td class="p-2">social_support</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n                </tbody>\n            </table>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n     \n    <style>\n            .guideline-html-content h1 {\n                font-size: 1.1rem;\n                font-weight: 800;\n                margin-bottom: 0.5rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h2 {\n                font-size: 1rem;\n                font-weight: 700;\n                margin-bottom: 0.4rem;\n                margin-top: 1rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h3 {\n                font-size: 0.9rem;\n                font-weight: 600;\n                margin-bottom: 0.3rem;\n                margin-top: 0.8rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content p {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content ul,\n            .guideline-html-content ol {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n                padding-left: 1.25rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content li {\n                margin-bottom: 0.2rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content strong {\n                font-weight: 700;\n                color: #1e293b;\n            }\n        </style> </div> 	You know, life in Kiambu’s estate is always busy for me. Every morning, I finish up with milking the cows, then I rush off to do deliveries in our neighbourhood, all while thinking about what I’ll eat later. Lately, when I come home after sunset, I find myself in the tiny kitchen, making a quick cup of chai and munching on soft chapati with a fat piece of cheese. I never really stop to check the time—or think if it’s too late for a meal. Last week, after a long day, I tried to wash the milk cans in my backyard, but my hands were shaky. Why did that tiny task feel so hard? Could my late-night snacking be making things worse?\n\nOne afternoon, after seeing me look tired, my neighbour Mama Muthoni—who works at the local clinic—called me over. At first, I almost pretended I was fine, but she just smiled and asked, ‘Wambui, do you sometimes skip meals then eat late at night?’ I nodded. ‘My dear, for diabetes and PCOS, eating late can push your sugar high and mess up your sleep. It’s better to eat small, regular meals early, and choose things like plain yogurt, boiled eggs, or porridge if you’re hungry at night.’ She even showed me simple stretches I could do right in my small living room and said, ‘Try fixing a healthy snack after work, instead of waiting till so late, eh?’ I wanted to believe her, but it sounded strange—do little changes like that really help?\n\nThat evening, I tried to follow her advice. I fixed myself a small bowl of millet porridge and skipped the big cheesy chapati. But as night grew quiet and I heard the neighbours’ radios, hunger tapped on my shoulder again. I stood by the fridge, tempted. Still, I remembered I had a big order of fresh milk for the local Women’s Guild coming up and wondered, will I really have more energy tomorrow if I keep trying? That thought helped me close the fridge, even if it wasn’t easy.\n\nA week later, to my surprise, I found myself feeling lighter in the mornings. My hands didn’t tremble as much, and washing the cans was quick. When the Women’s Guild ladies arrived, I happily carried every jug with a steady step. Maybe it only takes one small change to open space for another. Now, I greet each day thinking, could I keep doing this for my health? I reckon I can, one bowl of porridge at a time.	{https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/c2a50ef7-ddbd-416c-89cf-f9a4ddc766da_0.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/c2a50ef7-ddbd-416c-89cf-f9a4ddc766da_1.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/c2a50ef7-ddbd-416c-89cf-f9a4ddc766da_2.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/c2a50ef7-ddbd-416c-89cf-f9a4ddc766da_3.png}	{https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/c2a50ef7-ddbd-416c-89cf-f9a4ddc766da_0.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/c2a50ef7-ddbd-416c-89cf-f9a4ddc766da_1.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/c2a50ef7-ddbd-416c-89cf-f9a4ddc766da_2.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/c2a50ef7-ddbd-416c-89cf-f9a4ddc766da_3.mp3}	I sometimes eat late at night. How does this affect my blood sugar, and what can I do instead? 	diet	female	overlapped	2026-03-01 15:11:12.239471+00	\N
