ol</td>\n                <td class="p-2">No</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">physical_activity</td>\n                <td class="p-2">1-2 days</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">diet_restrictions</td>\n                <td class="p-2">Halal</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">support_network</td>\n                <td class="p-2">Healthcare provider or counsellor</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">Question</td>\n                <td class="p-2">Can I just walk for exercise, or should I do other types too?</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">generated_queries</td>\n                <td class="p-2">[\n  &quot;What are some traditional Hausa dishes available in Kano city that are suitable for a female trader with type 2 diabetes following a Kosher diet?&quot;,\n  &quot;How does weekly tobacco smoking impact blood sugar management in middle-aged Muslim women with type 2 diabetes living in urban Nigeria?&quot;,\n  &quot;Where can I find diabetes-friendly meal options near major markets in Kano if I often have easy access to fresh foods but need to avoid eating late at night?&quot;,\n  &quot;Are there any local support groups for Hausa women with diabetes in Kano who work as traders and want to share stories and experiences?&quot;,\n  &quot;What practical ways can urban female traders in Kano balance socialising with family and friends while managing type 2 diabetes, especially regarding shared meals and late-night gatherings?&quot;,\n  &quot;How should I adjust my insulin or oral medication if I occasionally eat late at night after coming home from the market in Kano?&quot;,\n  &quot;Are herbal or traditional medicines commonly used among Hausa Muslim women in Kano for diabetes, and do they interact with standard diabetes medications like Metformin?&quot;,\n  &quot;What are culturally appropriate exercises or physical activities for busy, middle-aged Hausa women in Kano with type 2 diabetes who currently only exercise 1-2 times per week?&quot;,\n  &quot;How does fasting during Ramadan affect blood sugar and medication schedules for working Muslim women with type 2 diabetes in Kano?&quot;,\n  &quot;Are there storytelling groups or events in Kano city that welcome women with diabetes looking to connect and unwind after a day at the market?&quot;,\n  &quot;What advice do local Kano healthcare clinics give to Muslim female tobacco smokers with diabetes who want to quit or reduce smoking to improve their health?&quot;,\n  &quot;Which local fruits and vegetables available in Kano&#x27;s markets are best for blood sugar control, given my easy access and preference for healthy foods?&quot;\n]</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">Category</td>\n                <td class="p-2">exercise</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">study_number</td>\n                <td class="p-2">f8f0a90b-c781-46e9-8d00-1b2c0ee1d951</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">health_goals</td>\n                <td class="p-2">Can I just walk for exercise, or should I do other types too?</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">output_format</td>\n                <td class="p-2">Text, Image and audio</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">type</td>\n                <td class="p-2">independent</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">parent</td>\n                <td class="p-2"></td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">label</td>\n                <td class="p-2">BAD</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">story_arc</td>\n                <td class="p-2">classic_change</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">output_tone</td>\n                <td class="p-2">classic_change</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n                </tbody>\n            </table>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n     \n    <style>\n            .guideline-html-content h1 {\n                font-size: 1.1rem;\n                font-weight: 800;\n                margin-bottom: 0.5rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h2 {\n                font-size: 1rem;\n                font-weight: 700;\n                margin-bottom: 0.4rem;\n                margin-top: 1rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h3 {\n                font-size: 0.9rem;\n                font-weight: 600;\n                margin-bottom: 0.3rem;\n                margin-top: 0.8rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content p {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content ul,\n            .guideline-html-content ol {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n                padding-left: 1.25rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content li {\n                margin-bottom: 0.2rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content strong {\n                font-weight: 700;\n                color: #1e293b;\n            }\n        </style> </div> 	So one Tuesday morning, my manager asked me to help restock shelves before opening. Easy, I thought, until my legs felt heavy and my body got sore before I finished half the work. Was it because I skipped breakfast and rushed out, or maybe it was the sweet tea? I brushed it off, thinking, 'Amina, you just need more sleep.' But deep inside, didn’t I wonder: why do my feet always get so sore? I sat on the stool behind the counter, embarrassed as another lady finished my job.\n\nSiphiwe, the clinic nurse, popped into the shop that afternoon. She greeted me, her eyes kind, and asked about my day. When I grumbled about my sore feet and tiredness, she didn’t shake her head. She said softly, 'Walking is good, Amina, but try adding simple stretches or a slow dance after supper – you’ll see a big change.' She explained, 'Just walking is fine for some, but the body likes it when we mix things up a bit. Walking, then stretching, and sometimes small weights – all halal, all at your own pace.' I wanted to say I was too busy, but she made it sound simple, not scary.\n\nThat night, I tried to follow her advice. I walked around the block after maghrib. My neighbour kids laughed, 'Are you training for Comrades, Amina?' I grinned back but felt shy. At home, I forgot how to do the stretches, so I just waved my arms in the kitchen, hoping nobody saw me. It felt silly, but I remembered the delivery at work the next day – a big one, not like the small packs. That kept me going.\n\nAfter four evenings of light walking and awkward stretches, I woke up feeling lighter – not perfect, but lighter. When the delivery truck roared up, I didn’t rush or panic. I lifted each box calm and steady, not out of breath, and even joked with my colleague. I realised, I’m not training for anything except my life. Maybe tomorrow I add five more minutes. Maybe one day I even teach the kids my funny kitchen dance. Change isn’t easy, but if I can do it, anyone in the neighbourhood can.	{https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/f8f0a90b-c781-46e9-8d00-1b2c0ee1d951_0.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/f8f0a90b-c781-46e9-8d00-1b2c0ee1d951_1.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/f8f0a90b-c781-46e9-8d00-1b2c0ee1d951_2.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/f8f0a90b-c781-46e9-8d00-1b2c0ee1d951_3.png}	{https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/f8f0a90b-c781-46e9-8d00-1b2c0ee1d951_0.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/f8f0a90b-c781-46e9-8d00-1b2c0ee1d951_1.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/f8f0a90b-c781-46e9-8d00-1b2c0ee1d951_2.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/f8f0a90b-c781-46e9-8d00-1b2c0ee1d951_3.mp3}	Can I just walk for exercise, or should I do other types too?	exercise	female	independent	2026-02-22 22:58:59.085737+00	\N
