 <td class="p-2 font-bold">alcohol</td>\n                <td class="p-2">No</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">physical_activity</td>\n                <td class="p-2">3-4 days</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">diet_restrictions</td>\n                <td class="p-2">Halal</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">support_network</td>\n                <td class="p-2">Healthcare provider or counsellor</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">Question</td>\n                <td class="p-2">Eating healthy can get expensive—how can I manage a nutritious diet on a tight budget? And can I still enjoy some traditional foods? </td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">generated_queries</td>\n                <td class="p-2">[\n  &quot;What are some Hausa cuisine dishes available in urban Sokoto that are suitable for a young Muslim woman with type 2 diabetes and Kosher dietary needs?&quot;,\n  &quot;Where can I find healthy, low-glycemic street food or restaurant options near me in Sokoto for someone managing type 2 diabetes?&quot;,\n  &quot;Are there Islamic-based support groups or spiritual resources in Sokoto for young female students with diabetes?&quot;,\n  &quot;How does high alcohol consumption impact blood sugar management for Muslim women in urban Nigeria with type 2 diabetes?&quot;,\n  &quot;What Qurâ€™an-inspired healthy lifestyle tips are relevant for young Hausa women living with type 2 diabetes in Nigerian cities?&quot;,\n  &quot;Which local Hausa foods commonly found in Sokoto markets are both Kosher and safe for type 2 diabetes?&quot;,\n  &quot;Are there any diabetes education workshops or counselling services tailored to young female students in Sokoto?&quot;,\n  &quot;How can I enjoy traditional Nigerian celebrations in Sokoto without causing blood sugar spikes or conflicting with my religious guidelines?&quot;,\n  &quot;What are examples of everyday physical activities popular among Hausa Muslim women in Sokoto that help manage diabetes?&quot;,\n  &quot;Are there any mobile apps or online platforms in Nigeria that help track blood sugar and diet, available in Hausa or English?&quot;,\n  &quot;How do other young, urban Muslim women in Nigeria balance spiritual practices, their studies, and type 2 diabetes management?&quot;,\n  &quot;What local herbal or traditional remedies are used in Sokoto for diabetes, and are they safe to combine with insulin or metformin?&quot;\n]</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">Category</td>\n                <td class="p-2">diet</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">study_number</td>\n                <td class="p-2">c21d88b8-b40b-487f-94ac-a2c18fffc081</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">health_goals</td>\n                <td class="p-2">Eating healthy can get expensive—how can I manage a nutritious diet on a tight budget? And can I still enjoy some traditional foods? </td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">output_format</td>\n                <td class="p-2">Text, Image and audio</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">type</td>\n                <td class="p-2">overlapped</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">parent</td>\n                <td class="p-2"></td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">label</td>\n                <td class="p-2">EXCELLENT</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">story_arc</td>\n                <td class="p-2">social_support</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">output_tone</td>\n                <td class="p-2">social_support</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n                </tbody>\n            </table>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n     \n    <style>\n            .guideline-html-content h1 {\n                font-size: 1.1rem;\n                font-weight: 800;\n                margin-bottom: 0.5rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h2 {\n                font-size: 1rem;\n                font-weight: 700;\n                margin-bottom: 0.4rem;\n                margin-top: 1rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h3 {\n                font-size: 0.9rem;\n                font-weight: 600;\n                margin-bottom: 0.3rem;\n                margin-top: 0.8rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content p {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content ul,\n            .guideline-html-content ol {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n                padding-left: 1.25rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content li {\n                margin-bottom: 0.2rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content strong {\n                font-weight: 700;\n                color: #1e293b;\n            }\n        </style> </div> 	Honestly, being Sakura, it’s not always easy. I’m an undergraduate in Sokoto, you see, with classes and Islamic studies almost every weekday. Some days I’m so hungry that I buy fried snacks from the campus vendor—maybe kuli-kuli and puff-puff—without thinking much how that affects my diabetes. Last week, I had to prepare notes for group discussion. My energy dropped halfway, my hands started feeling shaky, and I just couldn’t finish in time. Imagine feeling that way with your classmates watching! I thought, ‘Isn’t simple food enough to keep me strong?’ But clearly, something wasn’t working.\n\nWhen I went for my regular check-up at the clinic, the nurse, Sister Rahila, noticed I looked tired. She sat with me and asked about what I was eating and how I was feeling. At first, I shrugged. I told her, ‘All food fills the stomach, there’s no difference.’ She just smiled gently and explained, ‘Sakura, your body is like a small generator. It needs proper fuel—especially with your insulin. Foods like tuwo shinkafa with miyan kuka, dan wake, steamed okra, grilled fish and leafy vegetables—that’s real fuel for you. Avoid too much fried dough—even if friends love it. Swap sugary drinks for kunun aya or water. Let’s make small, smart changes, eh?’ It sounded possible, but still, I wondered if I could really manage it daily.\n\nBack at hostel, I tried bringing bean dumplings and steamed greens instead of fried snacks. Old habits die hard! My roommate teased me, and honestly, I missed the usual quick bites. During a group study session, I reached for kuli-kuli out of habit, but then quickly switched to some cucumber slices. It wasn’t easy, but I kept telling myself—exams are coming, and I want to be focused and strong for all my tasks. I remembered Sister Rahila’s words, so I carried on.\n\nSlowly, things improved. My energy felt steadier, and I could finish all my class notes and even join in for after-class prayers. One day, I volunteered first in a big group presentation—and I didn’t feel tired at all! My classmates even asked about my lunch choices, and I really felt I could help them too. Now, I’m not perfect, but I want to keep learning small ways to stay healthy—tuwo, dan wake, and all. Maybe healthy eating isn’t just about me. Who would have thought?	{https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/c21d88b8-b40b-487f-94ac-a2c18fffc081_0.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/c21d88b8-b40b-487f-94ac-a2c18fffc081_1.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/c21d88b8-b40b-487f-94ac-a2c18fffc081_2.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/c21d88b8-b40b-487f-94ac-a2c18fffc081_3.png}	{https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/c21d88b8-b40b-487f-94ac-a2c18fffc081_0.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/c21d88b8-b40b-487f-94ac-a2c18fffc081_1.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/c21d88b8-b40b-487f-94ac-a2c18fffc081_2.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/c21d88b8-b40b-487f-94ac-a2c18fffc081_3.mp3}	Eating healthy can get expensive—how can I manage a nutritious diet on a tight budget? And can I still enjoy some traditional foods? 	diet	female	overlapped	2026-02-22 22:58:59.435208+00	\N
