 font-bold">alcohol</td>\n                <td class="p-2">No</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">physical_activity</td>\n                <td class="p-2">1-2 days</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">diet_restrictions</td>\n                <td class="p-2">Halal</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">support_network</td>\n                <td class="p-2">Healthcare provider or counsellor</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">Question</td>\n                <td class="p-2">I sometimes eat late at night. How does this affect my blood sugar, and what can I do instead? </td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">generated_queries</td>\n                <td class="p-2">[\n  &quot;What are some affordable and easy-to-prepare, Hausa-inspired meals suitable for a female retail trader in urban Kano living with type 2 diabetes and hypertension?&quot;,\n  &quot;How can women in Kano city who are working adults and observe Islamic dietary practices (including kosher) manage healthy eating for type 2 diabetes during Ramadan?&quot;,\n  &quot;Are there local Kano markets or supermarkets where I can buy healthy, diabetic-friendly foods compatible with Hausa cuisine and kosher restrictions?&quot;,\n  &quot;What sample daily meal plans consider both hypertension and type 2 diabetes for adult Hausa Muslim women in Northern Nigerian cities?&quot;,\n  &quot;What are some traditional Hausa recipes from Kano that can be adapted for healthy eating with diabetes, using ingredients commonly found in urban areas?&quot;,\n  &quot;How do I balance diabetes- and hypertension-friendly diets with regular Qurâ€™an recitation schedules and other spiritual activities as a busy retail trader in Kano?&quot;,\n  &quot;What lifestyle changes are recommended for urban Hausa Muslim women with easy access to healthy foods but who only get 1-2 days of physical activity weekly?&quot;,\n  &quot;Are there community support groups or healthcare programs in urban Kano providing dietary guidance specifically for female retail traders with type 2 diabetes?&quot;,\n  &quot;What are the risks and benefits of using herbal or traditional medicine for diabetes alongside oral medications in Kano, Nigeria, and what do local clinics advise?&quot;,\n  &quot;Which healthy, quick meal options are acceptable during work hours for Hausa Muslim women with dietary restrictions in Kano city?&quot;,\n  &quot;How can I reduce my rare tobacco smoking to better manage type 2 diabetes and hypertension within the cultural context of Kano and the Hausa community?&quot;,\n  &quot;Are there any Islamic teachings or local Imam advice in Kano related to managing chronic health conditions like diabetes through diet and lifestyle?&quot;  \n]</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">Category</td>\n                <td class="p-2">diet</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">study_number</td>\n                <td class="p-2">ec923ec1-df1d-410a-9777-20475b7524ef</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">health_goals</td>\n                <td class="p-2">I sometimes eat late at night. How does this affect my blood sugar, and what can I do instead? </td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">output_format</td>\n                <td class="p-2">Text, Image and audio</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">type</td>\n                <td class="p-2">overlapped</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">parent</td>\n                <td class="p-2"></td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">label</td>\n                <td class="p-2">EXCELLENT</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">story_arc</td>\n                <td class="p-2">social_support</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">output_tone</td>\n                <td class="p-2">social_support</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n                </tbody>\n            </table>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n     \n    <style>\n            .guideline-html-content h1 {\n                font-size: 1.1rem;\n                font-weight: 800;\n                margin-bottom: 0.5rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h2 {\n                font-size: 1rem;\n                font-weight: 700;\n                margin-bottom: 0.4rem;\n                margin-top: 1rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h3 {\n                font-size: 0.9rem;\n                font-weight: 600;\n                margin-bottom: 0.3rem;\n                margin-top: 0.8rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content p {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content ul,\n            .guideline-html-content ol {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n                padding-left: 1.25rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content li {\n                margin-bottom: 0.2rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content strong {\n                font-weight: 700;\n                color: #1e293b;\n            }\n        </style> </div> 	My name is Amina Yusuf, and my daily life in Kano is always busy! As a trader in the market, I’m on my feet from sunrise to Maghrib, selling cloth and chatting with customers. Sometimes when I close late, hunger catches me, and I eat tuwo shinkafa or rice with miyan kuka before bed. I used to think, ah, what’s the harm? But last week, I was so tired at work—my hands were shaking, and I got snappy with a customer over small change. How will I sell well when my body feels like that? I didn’t even finish arranging my new stock before one neighbor trader, Rabi, stopped by to ask if everything was alright.\n\nWhen things didn’t get better, I decided to visit the clinic near Sabon Gari. Nurse Zainab, gentle but firm, listened while I explained my late-night eating, my medicine, and how I feel tired every morning. She smiled and said, 'Amina, eating heavy food late can make your blood sugar go up and keep you tired. Try eating your main meal early, before Maghrib, and have only a small, healthy snack if you’re hungry at night. Dan wake with spinach sauce, or a small bowl of millet porridge with groundnut, is better than a big plate of rice. You’ll feel lighter, and your sugar will stay steady.' I nodded, though in my mind I was still not sure. Habits are not easy to change, ba haka bane?\n\nThe next evening, I tried Nurse Zainab’s advice. I packed my healthy dan wake for dinner and left the big tuwo in the pot. But as work dragged on and my friends started talking about masa with pepper stew, my mouth watered! I almost gave in, but I remembered there was a meeting the next day in the market—something big about a new supplier, and I needed my mind clear, no mistakes. So, I stuck with my small plate, but later, I tossed and turned, stomach rumbling. Change felt slow. How do people do this every day?\n\nAfter a few days, things felt better. My energy in the morning returned, and even my customers noticed I smiled more. When the supplier finally came, I managed to speak with confidence, calculate bills without mistake, and close a good deal for my shop. Now, I actually look forward to planning my healthy meals. I won’t say it’s easy, but I see that little by little, I can change—and it’s helping both my business and my body. And who knows? Maybe soon I’ll help the women next to me do the same.	{https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/ec923ec1-df1d-410a-9777-20475b7524ef_0.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/ec923ec1-df1d-410a-9777-20475b7524ef_1.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/ec923ec1-df1d-410a-9777-20475b7524ef_2.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/ec923ec1-df1d-410a-9777-20475b7524ef_3.png}	{https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/ec923ec1-df1d-410a-9777-20475b7524ef_0.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/ec923ec1-df1d-410a-9777-20475b7524ef_1.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/ec923ec1-df1d-410a-9777-20475b7524ef_2.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/ec923ec1-df1d-410a-9777-20475b7524ef_3.mp3}	I sometimes eat late at night. How does this affect my blood sugar, and what can I do instead? 	diet	female	overlapped	2026-02-22 22:58:59.809215+00	\N
