cal activities for diabetes control?&quot;,\n  &quot;What is a typical daily menu for a young urban Hausa Muslim woman observing halal dietary restrictions and managing type 2 diabetes?&quot;,\n  &quot;How can I incorporate my love for singing and praise poetry into stress management or mindfulness exercises that benefit my diabetes health?&quot;,\n  &quot;Which herbal or traditional medicines commonly used in Kano are considered safe for women with type 2 diabetes, and how can I discuss these with healthcare providers?&quot;,\n  &quot;Are there accessible nutrition workshops or diabetes education programs at clinics or mosques in urban Kano specifically for women my age?&quot;,\n  &quot;What are some common barriers that young working women in Kano face when trying to maintain a diabetes-friendly halal diet, and how can I overcome them?&quot;\n]</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">Category</td>\n                <td class="p-2">diet</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">study_number</td>\n                <td class="p-2">f09e07af-83b6-471e-bd0d-76376dad22ce</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">health_goals</td>\n                <td class="p-2">I like to snack—what are some healthy options and how often should I have them?</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">output_format</td>\n                <td class="p-2">Text, Image and audio</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">type</td>\n                <td class="p-2">overlapped</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">parent</td>\n                <td class="p-2"></td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">label</td>\n                <td class="p-2">EXCELLENT</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">story_arc</td>\n                <td class="p-2">social_support</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">output_tone</td>\n                <td class="p-2">social_support</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n                </tbody>\n            </table>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n     \n    <style>\n            .guideline-html-content h1 {\n                font-size: 1.1rem;\n                font-weight: 800;\n                margin-bottom: 0.5rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h2 {\n                font-size: 1rem;\n                font-weight: 700;\n                margin-bottom: 0.4rem;\n                margin-top: 1rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h3 {\n                font-size: 0.9rem;\n                font-weight: 600;\n                margin-bottom: 0.3rem;\n                margin-top: 0.8rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content p {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content ul,\n            .guideline-html-content ol {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n                padding-left: 1.25rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content li {\n                margin-bottom: 0.2rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content strong {\n                font-weight: 700;\n                color: #1e293b;\n            }\n        </style> </div> 	Yesterday morning, I got up hungry because I stayed up late writing a praise poem for my religious group. My head felt heavy, but I had no time, so I grabbed bread and fried kosai on my way to Sabon Gari Market. As I prepared my little stall, answering customers and sorting wares, my hand started shaking. Eh, have you ever had your hand shake and the whole crowd watch you with those curious eyes? The small work of arranging fabric piles took so long because I felt weak, and I had to sit down just as customers were coming.\n\nLater, the health worker from the community hospital passed by. She saw my struggle and sat beside me, gentle as a sister. I said, "I just need quick strength, maybe more amala or bread, ba damuwa, I’m strong." She shook her head and smiled, asking, "Amina, what you eat for snacks, does it fill you or drop you?" She explained how groundnuts, unsweetened yogurt, small fruit slices, or even moi-moi could give lasting energy without spiking sugar—they are halal, simple, and found right here in the market. She told me to eat these as snacks, three times a day, and in small handfuls, not a big load. As she left, she promised, "Try it for just a week before the praise night next Saturday." But in my heart, I worried. Could nuts and yogurt be better than my sweet buns?\n\nThe next day I packed groundnuts, a little sliced pawpaw, and unsweetened yogurt into my bag before going out. My hand almost reached for the sweet doughnut at the tea stall, but I remembered the health worker’s advice and pulled my snacks out. By afternoon, I started missing the soft, sugary taste. I almost gave up when my friend Halima brought masa dripping in honey. But then I thought of the big group praise poetry event coming, and how I wanted to sing strong and clear on stage. So, I took a deep breath, nibbled my groundnuts slowly, and hummed a song instead.\n\nBy the weekend, my body felt lighter and my voice was stronger. On praise night, I stood with other sisters, smiling proud. My energy held as I sang, no shakiness, no sweat drops from hunger. People cheered—all I could do was laugh. Could it be small snacks that brought me here? Yes, wallahi, it was. Now, I’m ready to use this snack wisdom every day. Isn’t health about what we choose, little by little? Today, I believe it is.	{https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/f09e07af-83b6-471e-bd0d-76376dad22ce_0.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/f09e07af-83b6-471e-bd0d-76376dad22ce_1.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/f09e07af-83b6-471e-bd0d-76376dad22ce_2.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/f09e07af-83b6-471e-bd0d-76376dad22ce_3.png}	{https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/f09e07af-83b6-471e-bd0d-76376dad22ce_0.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/f09e07af-83b6-471e-bd0d-76376dad22ce_1.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/f09e07af-83b6-471e-bd0d-76376dad22ce_2.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/f09e07af-83b6-471e-bd0d-76376dad22ce_3.mp3}	I like to snack—what are some healthy options and how often should I have them?	diet	female	overlapped	2026-02-22 22:59:00.205619+00	\N
