   <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">tobacco</td>\n                <td class="p-2">No</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">alcohol</td>\n                <td class="p-2">No</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">physical_activity</td>\n                <td class="p-2">0 days</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">diet_restrictions</td>\n                <td class="p-2">Vegan</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">support_network</td>\n                <td class="p-2">Close friends</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">Question</td>\n                <td class="p-2">Can I just walk for exercise, or should I do other types too?</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">generated_queries</td>\n                <td class="p-2">[\n  &quot;What are some easy vegetarian meal ideas using locally available foods in urban areas of the Eastern Cape for someone with type 2 diabetes and hypertension?&quot;,\n  &quot;Are there isiXhosa-inspired vegetarian recipes suitable for a diabetic diet that I can prepare at home in the city?&quot;,\n  &quot;How can a working female teacher aged 55–64 in the Eastern Cape manage healthy eating with a busy schedule and easy access to urban food options?&quot;,\n  &quot;What are some culturally appropriate snacks that align with Christian (African Independent Churches) practices and are diabetes-friendly?&quot;,\n  &quot;Can you suggest a sample day’s menu for a vegetarian with hypertension and type 2 diabetes that incorporates local Eastern Cape produce?&quot;,\n  &quot;How do local Eastern Cape urban supermarkets support vegetarian and diabetic-friendly shopping?&quot;,\n  &quot;Are there gospel music groups or events in Eastern Cape urban areas that promote wellness or provide support for women managing diabetes?&quot;,\n  &quot;What are some gentle physical activities suitable for a 55–64 year old woman with type 2 diabetes and hypertension who currently does no regular exercise?&quot;,\n  &quot;How do local clinics in Eastern Cape cities support diabetic medication management, specifically for those using insulin injections, oral medication, and traditional remedies?&quot;,\n  &quot;Are there support groups in isiXhosa communities or churches in the Eastern Cape for women managing type 2 diabetes?&quot;,\n  &quot;How can I integrate spiritual or religious routines with healthy lifestyle changes as an urban isiXhosa woman?&quot;,\n  &quot;What local herbs or traditional medicines are safe and effective for managing type 2 diabetes alongside western medications in South Africa&#x27;s Eastern Cape?&quot;\n]</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">Category</td>\n                <td class="p-2">exercise</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">study_number</td>\n                <td class="p-2">f7e58396-00d3-4d70-add9-e7b60baf2cd9</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">health_goals</td>\n                <td class="p-2">Can I just walk for exercise, or should I do other types too?</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">output_format</td>\n                <td class="p-2">Text, Image and audio</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">type</td>\n                <td class="p-2">control</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">parent</td>\n                <td class="p-2"></td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">label</td>\n                <td class="p-2">EXCELLENT</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">story_arc</td>\n                <td class="p-2">resistance</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">output_tone</td>\n                <td class="p-2">resistance</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n                </tbody>\n            </table>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n     \n    <style>\n            .guideline-html-content h1 {\n                font-size: 1.1rem;\n                font-weight: 800;\n                margin-bottom: 0.5rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h2 {\n                font-size: 1rem;\n                font-weight: 700;\n                margin-bottom: 0.4rem;\n                margin-top: 1rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h3 {\n                font-size: 0.9rem;\n                font-weight: 600;\n                margin-bottom: 0.3rem;\n                margin-top: 0.8rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content p {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content ul,\n            .guideline-html-content ol {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n                padding-left: 1.25rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content li {\n                margin-bottom: 0.2rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content strong {\n                font-weight: 700;\n                color: #1e293b;\n            }\n        </style> </div> 	I woke up on a chilly morning in East London, ready for school, and packed my usual oats with apple for breakfast. The night before, I was tired and didn’t finish my lesson plan, thinking I could do it quickly before class. When I arrived, my hands shook a little and my head was sore. I went straight into work anyway. Eish, why did I skip my morning snack? That lesson flopped—my mind was slow, and I even snapped at the children. Can you believe a simple thing like a snack can mess up an entire class?\n\nThat afternoon, Sister Nomsa at the clinic called about my blood pressure. I went there with my arms folded and listened as she explained kindly, 'Walking is good, Sisi-Sinethemba, but even 10 minutes can make a difference. Just start with a stroll after school. You don’t have to run marathons! Plan your meals, pack snacks, and try to move—even singing along to gospel while you tidy counts.' She gave me a flyer with isiXhosa veggie recipes that reminded me of home, and said, 'Mix tradition with new habits—uzobona!' I nodded but, hayi, I wasn’t sure it would really work.\n\nAfter the clinic visit, I tried to fit in a short walk in the garden after school. It felt strange, and I kept looking around, worried someone would laugh—it’s not what I’m used to. That first day, I couldn’t finish grading my pile of books. My mind drifted back to wanting to flop onto the couch with amaGospel CDs instead. But I kept thinking about next week’s big school event, how everyone would be watching me lead assembly. I didn’t want to look tired and slow again!\n\nSlowly, I made walking a habit, step by little step. I started to pack my bean salad in bright bowls and walked quietly around the block, humming 'Nkosi sikelel' iAfrika' to steady my legs. When the big assembly day came, I stood tall, breathed deeply, and felt stronger—even remembering to smile at every learner. When I finished speaking without blanking out or snapping, I knew: maybe walking isn’t magic, but it’s working for me. Now, honestly, maybe I’ll try another activity soon—after all, who said old dogs can’t learn new tricks?	{https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/f7e58396-00d3-4d70-add9-e7b60baf2cd9_0.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/f7e58396-00d3-4d70-add9-e7b60baf2cd9_1.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/f7e58396-00d3-4d70-add9-e7b60baf2cd9_2.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/f7e58396-00d3-4d70-add9-e7b60baf2cd9_3.png}	{https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/f7e58396-00d3-4d70-add9-e7b60baf2cd9_0.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/f7e58396-00d3-4d70-add9-e7b60baf2cd9_1.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/f7e58396-00d3-4d70-add9-e7b60baf2cd9_2.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/f7e58396-00d3-4d70-add9-e7b60baf2cd9_3.mp3}	Can I just walk for exercise, or should I do other types too?	exercise	female	control	2026-02-22 23:02:42.052378+00	\N
