-2 font-bold">tobacco</td>\n                <td class="p-2">No</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">alcohol</td>\n                <td class="p-2">Yes</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">physical_activity</td>\n                <td class="p-2">3–4 days</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">diet_restrictions</td>\n                <td class="p-2">Vegetarian</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">support_network</td>\n                <td class="p-2">I live alone or have limited support</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">Question</td>\n                <td class="p-2">How often and how long should I exercise to actually improve my health?</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">generated_queries</td>\n                <td class="p-2">[\n  &quot;What are some affordable IsiXhosa-inspired, Halal-friendly meals available in urban Eastern Cape that are suitable for someone managing type 2 diabetes?&quot;,\n  &quot;Where can I find local Eastern Cape support groups or community activities for women over 55 living with diabetes and anxiety, especially for those with limited family support?&quot;,\n  &quot;Which fruits and vegetables commonly sold at supermarkets or local markets in [insert major Eastern Cape city] are lowest on the glycemic index?&quot;,\n  &quot;How can I incorporate traditional storytelling (iintsomi) and praise poetry (izibongo) into group activities to reduce social isolation and support mental health as a diabetic elder?&quot;,\n  &quot;Are there any physical activity programs in my city (Eastern Cape urban area) tailored for women 55+ with type 2 diabetes that meet 3–4 times per week?&quot;,\n  &quot;What local herbal or traditional remedies are commonly used by IsiXhosa women for managing blood sugar, and are they safe to combine with insulin or Metformin?&quot;,\n  &quot;Which everyday Halal snacks available in Eastern Cape shops won&#x27;t cause blood sugar spikes?&quot;,\n  &quot;Where can I access free or affordable mental health resources in an Eastern Cape urban area if I struggle with anxiety or depression linked to diabetes?&quot;,\n  &quot;How can urban living in the Eastern Cape impact access to fresh, healthy foods for people with diabetes, and what are practical shopping tips for my area?&quot;,\n  &quot;What are the best IsiXhosa praise poetry examples focusing on living with chronic illness that I can share with my students?&quot;,\n  &quot;Which local restaurants in my city offer diabetic-friendly, Halal meals suitable for someone my age who enjoys socializing with friends or family?&quot;,\n  &quot;What strategies are recommended for urban-dwelling, agnostic, Xhosa women living alone to maintain consistent diabetes self-care and medication routines?&quot;\n]</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">Category</td>\n                <td class="p-2">exercise</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">study_number</td>\n                <td class="p-2">0b910dd0-2012-4c73-ad31-391c6f95558c</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">health_goals</td>\n                <td class="p-2">How often and how long should I exercise to actually improve my health?</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">output_format</td>\n                <td class="p-2">Text, Image and audio</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">type</td>\n                <td class="p-2">independent</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">parent</td>\n                <td class="p-2"></td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">label</td>\n                <td class="p-2">BAD</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">story_arc</td>\n                <td class="p-2">classic_change</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">output_tone</td>\n                <td class="p-2">classic_change</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n                </tbody>\n            </table>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n     \n    <style>\n            .guideline-html-content h1 {\n                font-size: 1.1rem;\n                font-weight: 800;\n                margin-bottom: 0.5rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h2 {\n                font-size: 1rem;\n                font-weight: 700;\n                margin-bottom: 0.4rem;\n                margin-top: 1rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h3 {\n                font-size: 0.9rem;\n                font-weight: 600;\n                margin-bottom: 0.3rem;\n                margin-top: 0.8rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content p {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content ul,\n            .guideline-html-content ol {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n                padding-left: 1.25rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content li {\n                margin-bottom: 0.2rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content strong {\n                font-weight: 700;\n                color: #1e293b;\n            }\n        </style> </div> 	One Monday morning, I wanted to sort out the office cupboard, just a small task before the big audit that is coming. I told myself, 'Sisanda, you can do this.' But after a few minutes, I started feeling tired, light-headed and needed to sit down. Why am I so tired? I ate pap and fried eggs before work, and took my morning medicine. Maybe I didn’t move enough over the weekend? I just thought, 'Maybe it’s me getting older.' So, I left the job for later. That night, I felt a little embarrassed. What if the big audit finds us unprepared?\n\nThat week, when I went to fetch my medicine at the clinic, I shared this with the nurse. She smiled and said, 'Sisanda, you need to move your body for at least 30 minutes, most days of the week. Walk fast, dance, or just go around your yard. If you can, do it four times a week. Exercise helps your diabetes and your mind.' I wanted to protest and say, 'But nurse, even walking is hard!' Still, she said kindly, 'It will get easier. Start small. Make it fun, like your izibongo. Even 10 minutes at a time helps. Do you want your body strong for your stories?' I nodded slowly.\n\nSo, after work, I put on my doek and old sneakers and started walking around our block, waving at the children. The first few days were not easy. My legs felt heavy, and sometimes I was short of breath. One afternoon, as I was walking, the neighbours laughed a little, and part of me wanted to hide inside. But I remembered the big audit next week—I want to be the strong Sisanda who finishes her work. I kept walking, step by step, even when my heart beat fast. 'If I can tell stories,' I thought, 'I can keep moving.'\n\nBit by bit, one week became two. I started to enjoy the fresh air and the greetings from people outside. My body was slowly waking up, and the tiredness was not so bad. When the audit day came, I finished organising without feeling out of breath. Even my boss clapped and gave me a smile. Now, when I walk or dance with the children, I feel more happy and light. Who knew that little steps would bring so much change? Now, I want to keep going—maybe even lead our lunch break dances at work!	{https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/0b910dd0-2012-4c73-ad31-391c6f95558c_0.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/0b910dd0-2012-4c73-ad31-391c6f95558c_1.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/0b910dd0-2012-4c73-ad31-391c6f95558c_2.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/0b910dd0-2012-4c73-ad31-391c6f95558c_3.png}	{https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/0b910dd0-2012-4c73-ad31-391c6f95558c_0.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/0b910dd0-2012-4c73-ad31-391c6f95558c_1.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/0b910dd0-2012-4c73-ad31-391c6f95558c_2.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/0b910dd0-2012-4c73-ad31-391c6f95558c_3.mp3}	How often and how long should I exercise to actually improve my health?	exercise	female	independent	2026-02-22 23:02:43.368746+00	\N
