, especially regarding meal timing and access to healthy vegan meals?&quot;,\n  &quot;Is there support from Kisumu healthcare clinics for vegan diet planning and blood sugar monitoring for Muslims who work irregular hours?&quot;,\n  &quot;What are the effects of eating ugali and sukuma wiki late at night for adults with diabetes and hypertension in urban Kenya?&quot;,\n  &quot;Are there any Luo cultural practices or beliefs about food and health that might influence my diabetes management?&quot;,\n  &quot;Where can I join local support groups or counselling services in Kisumu for young men living with diabetes and limited food options?&quot;,\n  &quot;How can I adjust my exercise routine in Kisumu city to fit my work schedule and improve my blood pressure and blood sugar control?&quot;\n]</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">Category</td>\n                <td class="p-2">diet</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">study_number</td>\n                <td class="p-2">995d4e82-41ce-47a1-87a9-d6898a72a519</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">health_goals</td>\n                <td class="p-2">Which everyday foods can I eat that won&#x27;t make my blood sugar spike?</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">output_format</td>\n                <td class="p-2">Text, Image and audio</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">type</td>\n                <td class="p-2">independent</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">parent</td>\n                <td class="p-2"></td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">label</td>\n                <td class="p-2">BAD</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">story_arc</td>\n                <td class="p-2">crisis_avoidance</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">output_tone</td>\n                <td class="p-2">crisis_avoidance</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n                </tbody>\n            </table>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n     \n    <style>\n            .guideline-html-content h1 {\n                font-size: 1.1rem;\n                font-weight: 800;\n                margin-bottom: 0.5rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h2 {\n                font-size: 1rem;\n                font-weight: 700;\n                margin-bottom: 0.4rem;\n                margin-top: 1rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h3 {\n                font-size: 0.9rem;\n                font-weight: 600;\n                margin-bottom: 0.3rem;\n                margin-top: 0.8rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content p {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content ul,\n            .guideline-html-content ol {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n                padding-left: 1.25rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content li {\n                margin-bottom: 0.2rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content strong {\n                font-weight: 700;\n                color: #1e293b;\n            }\n        </style> </div> 	You know, every morning I wake up in my little room here in the township, and right away I start thinking about climbing on my bicycle to deliver the bags of maize flour at the market. Most days, I just drink strong tea with two mandazi because it’s quick and easy. Maybe I grab a bit of leftover ugali, you know? But lately, after breakfast I feel so tired and dizzy – sometimes I even drop the small parcels or get to work late! I keep asking myself: why does my body feel like it’s fighting me when I need to focus? Isn’t food supposed to give me energy?\n\nOn Tuesday, Sister Mary from the clinic saw me sitting outside, holding my head after nearly dropping the bread delivery. She came over and asked, ‘Amani, have you checked your sugar today?’ I shrugged and tried to laugh it off, but she sat next to me and explained simply, ‘Baba, the mandazi and sweet tea are making your blood sugar jump high and fall again, that’s why you feel tired. Try brown bread, some beans, boiled eggs, or even sukuma wiki with a bit of ugali. It will help your blood and give you strength for work. Just little by little, make the change.’ Honestly, I wasn’t sure – how will I give up mandazi, my morning friend?\n\nSo, next morning, I boiled some eggs and made sukuma wiki like Sister Mary said, even though it felt strange – where’s the taste, where’s the sugar? My stomach grumbled, and my tongue missed the mandazi sweetness. I nearly gave up and went back to old habits, but then I remembered I have to deliver a heavy sack for Mama Ochieng’s shop tomorrow – if I’m weak, how will I manage? I told myself, just finish today, see what happens.\n\nA few days go by, and you won’t believe – I start feeling lighter, not so dizzy anymore. My hands don’t shake as I cycle to the market to deliver that heavy load. Mama Ochieng cheers me on, and I finish all the work before midday, strong and sweating like a proper worker. I smile to myself. Maybe, just maybe, I can keep this up, keep listening, and make it even better for me and my family.	{https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/995d4e82-41ce-47a1-87a9-d6898a72a519_0.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/995d4e82-41ce-47a1-87a9-d6898a72a519_1.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/995d4e82-41ce-47a1-87a9-d6898a72a519_2.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/995d4e82-41ce-47a1-87a9-d6898a72a519_3.png}	{https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/995d4e82-41ce-47a1-87a9-d6898a72a519_0.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/995d4e82-41ce-47a1-87a9-d6898a72a519_1.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/995d4e82-41ce-47a1-87a9-d6898a72a519_2.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/995d4e82-41ce-47a1-87a9-d6898a72a519_3.mp3}	Which everyday foods can I eat that won't make my blood sugar spike?	diet	male	independent	2026-02-24 14:11:09.711115+00	\N
