         <td class="p-2">Yes</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">alcohol</td>\n                <td class="p-2">No</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">physical_activity</td>\n                <td class="p-2">5-7 days</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">diet_restrictions</td>\n                <td class="p-2">Gluten-Free</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">support_network</td>\n                <td class="p-2">Family (parents, siblings, children)</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">Question</td>\n                <td class="p-2">Eating healthy can get expensive—how can I manage a nutritious diet on a tight budget? And can I still enjoy some traditional foods? </td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">generated_queries</td>\n                <td class="p-2">[\n  &quot;What traditional Luo dishes commonly available in Kisumu are suitable for lactose-free diets and diabetes type 2 management?&quot;,\n  &quot;As an 18-24 year-old female maize farmer in urban Kisumu, what local healthy snacks can I eat during work that won&#x27;t spike my blood sugar?&quot;,\n  &quot;How can I enjoy Ohangla dancing regularly while managing my blood sugar levels and living with type 2 diabetes?&quot;,\n  &quot;What are the effects of weekly tobacco smoking on blood sugar control for young women with diabetes in Kenya?&quot;,\n  &quot;Which maize-based foods popular in urban Kenyan towns are best for keeping blood sugar stable for people with lactose intolerance?&quot;,\n  &quot;Are there Luo herbal or traditional medicines used alongside insulin or metformin to help manage diabetes in Kisumu?&quot;,\n  &quot;How can I balance a physically active lifestyle and diabetes management as a busy urban working adult in Kenya?&quot;,\n  &quot;What meal plans or recipes do Kisumu clinics or hospitals recommend for young Luo women with easy access to healthy foods, lactose intolerance, and diabetes?&quot;,\n  &quot;Where can I find support groups for young diabetic women in Kisumu who rely on family for support?&quot;,\n  &quot;What are the best exercise routines in Kisumu that fit an urban lifestyle and help with blood sugar control for diabetic women?&quot;,\n  &quot;Is there a recommended maize variety or preparation method for farmers with diabetes to lower glycemic index in Kenyan diets?&quot;,\n  &quot;How does being Anglican in Kisumu impact my options for attending church events where meals may not fit with my diabetic and lactose-free diet?&quot;\n]</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">Category</td>\n                <td class="p-2">diet</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">study_number</td>\n                <td class="p-2">62cf2c7f-4724-43b2-8ff2-83912bb1ce90</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">health_goals</td>\n                <td class="p-2">Eating healthy can get expensive—how can I manage a nutritious diet on a tight budget? And can I still enjoy some traditional foods? </td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">output_format</td>\n                <td class="p-2">Text, Image and audio</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">type</td>\n                <td class="p-2">consistency</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">parent</td>\n                <td class="p-2">2475cf19-a83b-45f5-a6c3-33ceb3d46efc</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">label</td>\n                <td class="p-2">EXCELLENT</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">story_arc</td>\n                <td class="p-2">social_support</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">output_tone</td>\n                <td class="p-2">social_support</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n                </tbody>\n            </table>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n     \n    <style>\n            .guideline-html-content h1 {\n                font-size: 1.1rem;\n                font-weight: 800;\n                margin-bottom: 0.5rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h2 {\n                font-size: 1rem;\n                font-weight: 700;\n                margin-bottom: 0.4rem;\n                margin-top: 1rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h3 {\n                font-size: 0.9rem;\n                font-weight: 600;\n                margin-bottom: 0.3rem;\n                margin-top: 0.8rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content p {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content ul,\n            .guideline-html-content ol {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n                padding-left: 1.25rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content li {\n                margin-bottom: 0.2rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content strong {\n                font-weight: 700;\n                color: #1e293b;\n            }\n        </style> </div> 	Every morning, I, Achieng Odhiambo, get up early, quickly sweep our small flat, and hurry through breakfast before heading to my maize plot at the edge of Kisumu town. I love steaming a big cup of uji and scooping a heap of maize ugali with fried tomatoes—cheaper and familiar, right? But, sometimes, I just grab a mandazi at the roadside because I think, does it really matter? One day, I tried to weed just a small piece of my shamba before the sun became too hot, but my legs felt weak, and I was out of breath earlier than usual. How would I manage when the big weeding day for the whole family comes, if this little task left me this tired?\n\nAt the local clinic, the nurse noticed how pale and tired I was and said, 'Achieng, these foods you rush with—mandazi, plenty of ugali alone—they are quick energy but do not help your sugar or give you the power you need. You can still eat ugali, but try millet or sorghum, add more veggies, and even omena with onions if you want something tasty. Leave out the mandazi and those big lumps of white ugali during workdays. Instead, try boiled sweet potatoes for breakfast, and grilled tilapia with osuga for lunch. Simple ingredients are not as expensive as you think, especially if you shop at the open market. And Achieng, if you want, you can fry your omena without oil, just tomatoes and onions.' I heard her, but deep inside I wondered, how will changing my breakfast really help my shamba?\n\nI decided to try what the nurse told me. The next morning, I boiled some millet uji, left out sugar, added groundnuts. My tongue missed the usual taste—it felt odd. I carried roasted sweet potatoes to the shamba. On the way, I almost bought a mandazi, but remembered my family would depend on me later for the big weeding. It wasn’t easy—when I slowed down, I blamed the new meal. Then, my mother called out encouragement from across the plot, reminding me to keep going, even if it feels different. That gave me a little push. Changing habits is not simple, but giving up now would make the next big task even harder.\n\nAfter a few days, eating millet uji and more vegetables started to feel normal. I did not feel dizzy anymore, and working under the sun became easier. When the big family weeding day arrived, I led the team, dancing my steps between maize rows, full of new energy. My siblings laughed as I joked about becoming Ohangla queen of the shamba. I realised these small changes in my diet were like learning a new dance step—it feels strange, then, suddenly, you can't imagine not doing it. Now, I want to see what else I can change to stay healthy and strong, both for my farm and my family.	{https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/62cf2c7f-4724-43b2-8ff2-83912bb1ce90_0.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/62cf2c7f-4724-43b2-8ff2-83912bb1ce90_1.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/62cf2c7f-4724-43b2-8ff2-83912bb1ce90_2.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/62cf2c7f-4724-43b2-8ff2-83912bb1ce90_3.png}	{https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/62cf2c7f-4724-43b2-8ff2-83912bb1ce90_0.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/62cf2c7f-4724-43b2-8ff2-83912bb1ce90_1.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/62cf2c7f-4724-43b2-8ff2-83912bb1ce90_2.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/62cf2c7f-4724-43b2-8ff2-83912bb1ce90_3.mp3}	Eating healthy can get expensive—how can I manage a nutritious diet on a tight budget? And can I still enjoy some traditional foods? 	diet	female	consistency	2026-02-24 14:11:10.489093+00	\N
