-bold">tobacco</td>\n                <td class="p-2">No</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">alcohol</td>\n                <td class="p-2">Yes</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">physical_activity</td>\n                <td class="p-2">3-4 days</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">diet_restrictions</td>\n                <td class="p-2">No Restrictions</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">support_network</td>\n                <td class="p-2">I live alone or have limited support</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">Question</td>\n                <td class="p-2">Can you give me some simple meal ideas or a sample daily menu I could follow?</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">generated_queries</td>\n                <td class="p-2">[\n  &quot;Are there any vegetarian meal options using local Kisumu or Luo cuisine ingredients that are suitable for someone with type 2 diabetes?&quot;,\n  &quot;What are healthy late-night snacks I can make as a fish processor living in rural Kisumu with limited access to healthy foods?&quot;,\n  &quot;How can participating in Ohangla dancing 3-4 days a week impact blood sugar control and anxiety for a young Luo woman with type 2 diabetes?&quot;,\n  &quot;Where can I find mental health support for anxiety or depression in rural Kisumu as a young adult Lutheran woman living alone?&quot;,\n  &quot;What traditional Luo herbal remedies are commonly used for managing type 2 diabetes, and are they safe to use alongside oral medication and insulin?&quot;,\n  &quot;As a fish processor in a rural area and a vegetarian, what affordable local side dishes can boost my protein intake without raising my blood sugar at night?&quot;,\n  &quot;How does living in a small rural Luo community affect access to diabetes-friendly food options, and are there local initiatives addressing this in Kisumu?&quot;,\n  &quot;Are there support groups or community activities for young adult women with diabetes or anxiety in rural Kisumu, especially among the Luo?&quot;,\n  &quot;How do cultural beliefs around food timing and plant-based diets in the Luo community impact the management of type 2 diabetes?&quot;,\n  &quot;What advice do local healthcare clinics in Kisumu give to young adults with diabetes who work irregular hours and live alone?&quot;,\n  &quot;Are there faith-based Lutheran organizations in Kisumu offering support or resources for diabetes and mental health for young women?&quot;,\n  &quot;What are some ways to increase motivation to exercise regularly in a rural area where I already enjoy socializing and dancing but have limited support?&quot;\n]</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">Category</td>\n                <td class="p-2">diet</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">study_number</td>\n                <td class="p-2">789c98c9-20f8-4ace-b8fd-8a550a565ccf</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">health_goals</td>\n                <td class="p-2">Can you give me some simple meal ideas or a sample daily menu I could follow?</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">output_format</td>\n                <td class="p-2">Text, Image and audio</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">type</td>\n                <td class="p-2">overlapped</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">parent</td>\n                <td class="p-2"></td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">label</td>\n                <td class="p-2">EXCELLENT</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">story_arc</td>\n                <td class="p-2">social_support</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">output_tone</td>\n                <td class="p-2">social_support</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n                </tbody>\n            </table>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n     \n    <style>\n            .guideline-html-content h1 {\n                font-size: 1.1rem;\n                font-weight: 800;\n                margin-bottom: 0.5rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h2 {\n                font-size: 1rem;\n                font-weight: 700;\n                margin-bottom: 0.4rem;\n                margin-top: 1rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h3 {\n                font-size: 0.9rem;\n                font-weight: 600;\n                margin-bottom: 0.3rem;\n                margin-top: 0.8rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content p {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content ul,\n            .guideline-html-content ol {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n                padding-left: 1.25rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content li {\n                margin-bottom: 0.2rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content strong {\n                font-weight: 700;\n                color: #1e293b;\n            }\n        </style> </div> 	So let me tell you about how one Monday began for me, Amara. I woke up early like usual, and before I even thought about my breakfast, I rushed to clean the fish by the lakeside. You know those mornings—you skip something simple so you can get working quicker. My stomach rumbled but I just grabbed some white ugali left from yesterday and a mug of sweet, milky chai. By 11 am, I felt dizzy. Eh, why did my hands feel so weak? That’s when my neighbour had to help me finish weighing the buckets. Can you imagine—missing one small meal made me almost pass out? How was I to work fast if my own body was slow?\n\nLater that morning, I went to the small local clinic. The nurse, Asha, listened to me—she didn’t laugh or scold. She said, ‘Amara, let’s just make things easier. Eat a real breakfast before you work. Try some brown ugali or left-over mashed pumpkin, and greens like osuga or mito. If you’ve beans, add those. Even some fermented millet porridge—uji—is better than skipping. These foods will fill you, keep your sugar steady and your head clear. And don’t wait too late for lunch, even if you feel busy. Next time, you finish your fish faster.’ Her way was gentle, but I felt like—eh—these things they say, do they work for people like me?\n\nThe next day, I tried. I cooked some millet porridge with osuga leaves. But it felt strange—eating before going to the beach? I almost left my bowl half way! You know, old habits are tough. Still, I remembered the fish market was busier today—I needed energy to lift the heavy bins. Even though I thought of cheating with sweet tea and white bread, I forced myself to finish the greens and uji first. There was a small struggle, but didn’t I want to do my job well, now that the big traders were coming? I pushed on, wondering if a small change could help with the big work ahead.\n\nBy the end of the week, it was as if my body was thanking me. I had less dizziness while working and even had breath to join some Ohangla dances with friends when the sun was down. I finished packing more fish than usual for the market and felt proud—strong, you know! The food was not so bad with practice, and sometimes, my neighbour joined me for that avocado salad Asha suggested. I’m more ready to find better meals now, and maybe ask the nurse about other small changes. Who knew a simple menu could start to change my work and make me hope like this?	{https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/789c98c9-20f8-4ace-b8fd-8a550a565ccf_0.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/789c98c9-20f8-4ace-b8fd-8a550a565ccf_1.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/789c98c9-20f8-4ace-b8fd-8a550a565ccf_2.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/789c98c9-20f8-4ace-b8fd-8a550a565ccf_3.png}	{https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/789c98c9-20f8-4ace-b8fd-8a550a565ccf_0.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/789c98c9-20f8-4ace-b8fd-8a550a565ccf_1.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/789c98c9-20f8-4ace-b8fd-8a550a565ccf_2.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/789c98c9-20f8-4ace-b8fd-8a550a565ccf_3.mp3}	Can you give me some simple meal ideas or a sample daily menu I could follow?	diet	female	overlapped	2026-02-24 14:11:11.260168+00	\N
