cal activity routines?&quot;,\n  &quot;Are there any mobile health apps or programs specifically for Kenyan women with type 2 diabetes that can help track exercise and medication?&quot;,\n  &quot;What cultural practices within the Luo community could affect exercise habits and diabetes management for women my age?&quot;,\n  &quot;How can I balance irregular alcohol consumption with managing type 2 diabetes, considering my rare alcohol use?&quot;,\n  &quot;What are the recommendations for insulin and oral medication timing in relation to exercise schedules for adults with type 2 diabetes in Kenya?&quot;,\n  &quot;Which traditional Luo herbal medicines are considered safe to use with insulin or metformin for diabetes and what do local health professionals recommend?&quot;\n]</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">Category</td>\n                <td class="p-2">exercise</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">study_number</td>\n                <td class="p-2">2462a93f-2aa0-41fe-8ce6-47695abb30c1</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">health_goals</td>\n                <td class="p-2">How often and how long should I exercise to actually improve my health?</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">output_format</td>\n                <td class="p-2">Text, Image and audio</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">type</td>\n                <td class="p-2">overlapped</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">parent</td>\n                <td class="p-2"></td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">label</td>\n                <td class="p-2">EXCELLENT</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">story_arc</td>\n                <td class="p-2">social_support</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">output_tone</td>\n                <td class="p-2">social_support</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n                </tbody>\n            </table>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n     \n    <style>\n            .guideline-html-content h1 {\n                font-size: 1.1rem;\n                font-weight: 800;\n                margin-bottom: 0.5rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h2 {\n                font-size: 1rem;\n                font-weight: 700;\n                margin-bottom: 0.4rem;\n                margin-top: 1rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h3 {\n                font-size: 0.9rem;\n                font-weight: 600;\n                margin-bottom: 0.3rem;\n                margin-top: 0.8rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content p {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content ul,\n            .guideline-html-content ol {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n                padding-left: 1.25rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content li {\n                margin-bottom: 0.2rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content strong {\n                font-weight: 700;\n                color: #1e293b;\n            }\n        </style> </div> 	One Monday morning, I was typing a proposal before a small team meeting. I made some uji with sweet potatoes and fresh avocado for breakfast—thinking that’s healthy enough, right? But after only 20 minutes, I felt so drained, sweat beading on my forehead even though it wasn’t hot. I finished just a single page. My hands shook, and I had to sit and rest, feeling silly. Wasn’t eating right supposed to be enough? Why could I not even type two pages today?\n\nIn the afternoon, Sister Janet, the nurse from my local clinic, called to check in. At first, I didn’t want to talk about exercise. Exercise always sounded tiring! But Sister Janet just laughed kindly and said, "Akinyi, even just 30 minutes of walking, three or four times a week, will make a big change for your blood sugar and energy. Dance your Ohangla in your sitting room, walk to your neighbours—just get moving. Try small steps, yes?" Her Luo accent made it all sound so easy, and she said I could start slow, and not worry if I just do some stretches while cooking.\n\nThat evening, I pulled on my kitenge skirt and tried dancing Ohangla—just like Sister Janet encouraged me. Eish, I stopped after ten minutes, heart beating fast and legs a bit heavy. I nearly gave up, thinking this is too much work. But then I remembered, next week, we have a community event where I need to stand and talk for a long time. I need to get a bit fit! So even when I felt embarrassed breathing hard, I promised myself to try again tomorrow.\n\nEvery day that week, I kept dancing Ohangla for a little longer, and sometimes walked to the local market instead of driving. It wasn’t always easy, but I started to feel lighter and happier. When the community event came, I stood up with energy and confidence through the whole presentation—everyone noticed, and I felt proud. Now, I want to keep improving my health, one day at a time. Who knows what else I could do if I just keep moving?	{https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/2462a93f-2aa0-41fe-8ce6-47695abb30c1_0.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/2462a93f-2aa0-41fe-8ce6-47695abb30c1_1.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/2462a93f-2aa0-41fe-8ce6-47695abb30c1_2.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/2462a93f-2aa0-41fe-8ce6-47695abb30c1_3.png}	{https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/2462a93f-2aa0-41fe-8ce6-47695abb30c1_0.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/2462a93f-2aa0-41fe-8ce6-47695abb30c1_1.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/2462a93f-2aa0-41fe-8ce6-47695abb30c1_2.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/2462a93f-2aa0-41fe-8ce6-47695abb30c1_3.mp3}	How often and how long should I exercise to actually improve my health?	exercise	female	overlapped	2026-02-24 14:11:11.600391+00	\N
