w does late-night eating affect blood sugar for post-menopausal women in Kenya who are on both oral and traditional diabetic medicines?&quot;,\n  &quot;What diabetes-friendly Luo traditional foods are suitable for vegetarians living in urban Kenyan areas?&quot;,\n  &quot;What local support networks or counselling services exist in Siaya for female professors with diabetes seeking peer or professional guidance?&quot;,\n  &quot;Are there safe and accessible physical activity groups or classes in urban Siaya suitable for women aged 55-64 with type 2 diabetes?&quot;,\n  &quot;What is the role of herbal or traditional medicines in managing type 2 diabetes among Luo women in urban Kenya, and how does this interact with prescribed medications like insulin and metformin?&quot;,\n  &quot;How can late-night storytelling sessions affect my blood sugar levels, and what healthier alternatives can I consider in my nightly routine?&quot;\n]</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">Category</td>\n                <td class="p-2">exercise</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">study_number</td>\n                <td class="p-2">6b459a44-e892-49cc-8675-ad9b7fc128d9</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">health_goals</td>\n                <td class="p-2">Sometimes I feel tired or discouraged—how can I stay motivated, and how does exercise help my blood sugar?</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">output_format</td>\n                <td class="p-2">Text, Image and audio</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">type</td>\n                <td class="p-2">overlapped</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">parent</td>\n                <td class="p-2"></td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">label</td>\n                <td class="p-2">EXCELLENT</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">story_arc</td>\n                <td class="p-2">social_support</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">output_tone</td>\n                <td class="p-2">social_support</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n                </tbody>\n            </table>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n     \n    <style>\n            .guideline-html-content h1 {\n                font-size: 1.1rem;\n                font-weight: 800;\n                margin-bottom: 0.5rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h2 {\n                font-size: 1rem;\n                font-weight: 700;\n                margin-bottom: 0.4rem;\n                margin-top: 1rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h3 {\n                font-size: 0.9rem;\n                font-weight: 600;\n                margin-bottom: 0.3rem;\n                margin-top: 0.8rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content p {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content ul,\n            .guideline-html-content ol {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n                padding-left: 1.25rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content li {\n                margin-bottom: 0.2rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content strong {\n                font-weight: 700;\n                color: #1e293b;\n            }\n        </style> </div> 	You know, every morning I wake up to the sound of boda bodas outside my window, the city already alive, calling my name—Achieng Odinga, the storytelling professor who always rushes! I hustle into my kitchen for a quick meal: maybe brown uji or tea with bread, and I barely have time to taste it before dashing out to my campus lecture. One day, I was supposed to finish a simple task: marking my students’ essays before lunch. But ah! My hands felt heavy, my head was sore—tell me, have you ever felt as tired as an old cow in the sun? Before I knew it, I had fallen asleep at my office table, and work just piled up.\n\nLater that afternoon, my favourite nurse, Mama Atieno, came to the staff room, gently asking, "Professor, how are you really?" I wanted to say "fine" but she could see my eyes were tired. She explained how keeping active—even a short walk—could help my blood sugar stay even, make my energy come back sharp-sharp! I hesitated, thinking, will a stroll around the quad really help more than my medicine? She smiled, “Achieng, exercise is like finding a sweet tale—sometimes the answer is simple. Walk with friends after lunch, keep it fun, and check your sugar. Little by little, you’ll see the difference.” I promised her I’d try.\n\nThe next morning, I wore my old blue leso and left my marking for later. I convinced one junior lecturer to walk with me around the college. But after five minutes, I wanted to turn back—my legs were tired, and the sweet aroma of samosas from the canteen almost made me quit! But then I remembered, the Dean wanted me to give a workshop next week, in front of all the new staff. Ah! I thought, how will I stand for that long if I feel drained like this? So I puffed and panted, but I kept walking.\n\nSlowly, that small walk became a habit. My afternoons grew brighter, like the Siaya sun on clean linen. By the time the workshop arrived, I felt stronger—like the story-mothers in my Luo clan. I taught the young lecturers with energy and not once did I yawn or feel dizzy. That night, I gave thanks. Now, whenever I feel tired or start losing hope, I remember: one small step led me to my grand story. And I laugh, knowing with God and a little movement, there’s nothing this Professor cannot do!	{https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/6b459a44-e892-49cc-8675-ad9b7fc128d9_0.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/6b459a44-e892-49cc-8675-ad9b7fc128d9_1.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/6b459a44-e892-49cc-8675-ad9b7fc128d9_2.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/6b459a44-e892-49cc-8675-ad9b7fc128d9_3.png}	{https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/6b459a44-e892-49cc-8675-ad9b7fc128d9_0.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/6b459a44-e892-49cc-8675-ad9b7fc128d9_1.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/6b459a44-e892-49cc-8675-ad9b7fc128d9_2.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/6b459a44-e892-49cc-8675-ad9b7fc128d9_3.mp3}	Sometimes I feel tired or discouraged—how can I stay motivated, and how does exercise help my blood sugar?	exercise	female	overlapped	2026-02-24 14:11:12.113488+00	\N
