s-friendly workouts?&quot;,\n  &quot;What herbal or traditional medicines are commonly used in Homa Bay by Luo women for diabetes, and how safe are they with insulin?&quot;,\n  &quot;What are the key challenges faced by young female maize farmers in Kenya in maintaining blood sugar control during the harvest season?&quot;,\n  &quot;How often should someone my age with Type 2 diabetes visit a local healthcare clinic in Homa Bay for check-ups?&quot;,\n  &quot;What culturally relevant strategies do Luo women use to balance farming work, social support from friends, and diabetes management?&quot;,\n  &quot;Are there any faith-based diabetes education resources available for members of African Independent Churches in Homa Bay?&quot;\n]</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">Category</td>\n                <td class="p-2">exercise</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">study_number</td>\n                <td class="p-2">e69297d5-4262-4d24-a0dc-f2b2444b9ea0</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">health_goals</td>\n                <td class="p-2">What kinds of exercises are safe and helpful for someone with diabetes?</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">output_format</td>\n                <td class="p-2">Text, Image and audio</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">type</td>\n                <td class="p-2">control</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">parent</td>\n                <td class="p-2"></td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">label</td>\n                <td class="p-2">EXCELLENT</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">story_arc</td>\n                <td class="p-2">resistance</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">output_tone</td>\n                <td class="p-2">resistance</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n                </tbody>\n            </table>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n     \n    <style>\n            .guideline-html-content h1 {\n                font-size: 1.1rem;\n                font-weight: 800;\n                margin-bottom: 0.5rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h2 {\n                font-size: 1rem;\n                font-weight: 700;\n                margin-bottom: 0.4rem;\n                margin-top: 1rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h3 {\n                font-size: 0.9rem;\n                font-weight: 600;\n                margin-bottom: 0.3rem;\n                margin-top: 0.8rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content p {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content ul,\n            .guideline-html-content ol {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n                padding-left: 1.25rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content li {\n                margin-bottom: 0.2rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content strong {\n                font-weight: 700;\n                color: #1e293b;\n            }\n        </style> </div> 	Every morning, I wake up early in Homa Bay, boil my big kettle of uji with maize, and check my shamba before the sun gets too hot. You know, sometimes I just grab my hoe and start weeding without even having breakfast. One day, I was trying to water the new maize shoots quickly before walking to the market, but halfway through, I felt dizzy and needed to sit under the mango tree. Could it be all this running up and down without eating right, or am I just overthinking things?\n\nThat afternoon, my friend Auma, who works at the clinic, passed by. She saw me sitting and said, 'Achieng, you are busy but your body is giving you signals. Why not come to the clinic for some advice, just to be sure?' At first, I wanted to brush her off. Who has time for advice when the weeds are growing? But she sat with me, explained in simple words how diabetes and exercise are friends not enemies. 'Start with walking, small stretches, and slow Ohangla moves. Always check your sugar before and after. And Achieng, never skip a meal before work!' It sounded easy, but could it really help?\n\nSo the next day I tried waking up, taking my early breakfast, checking my sugar, and then stretching like Auma showed me. I walked with purpose across the field this time, but it felt strange and slow; I wanted to rush like before. By lunchtime, I was tired but not dizzy. Even so, changing old habits felt odd. Still, I kept thinking about that big market day coming up, when I'd need energy to sell all my maize.\n\nDay by day, I found myself feeling stronger. My shamba work went smoother, and my Ohangla dance steps in the evening made me laugh again. On market day, I was not only standing tall and selling with energy, but I was also teaching my friends small exercises to do when tired. Now, I feel ready to keep learning and get even healthier. Who said change can't be sweet?	{https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/e69297d5-4262-4d24-a0dc-f2b2444b9ea0_0.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/e69297d5-4262-4d24-a0dc-f2b2444b9ea0_1.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/e69297d5-4262-4d24-a0dc-f2b2444b9ea0_2.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/e69297d5-4262-4d24-a0dc-f2b2444b9ea0_3.png}	{https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/e69297d5-4262-4d24-a0dc-f2b2444b9ea0_0.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1