\n\nThe next day, the community health worker, Mama Susan, saw me sweating and sitting under the big mango tree, trying to catch my breath. She came over and asked, ‘Obiero, have you checked your exercise routine, or do you just do it to finish?’ I told her, ‘I just do what I do, because that’s what I know.’ She laughed softly and said, ‘Let me help you, my friend. All you need is 30 minutes of real exercise, five days a week—walking fast, riding your bicycle, or even strong cleaning. It must make your heart beat faster. And, always drink water, eat ugali and greens, and do not stop if it feels tough the first week. That is how you keep strong, bwana.’ I wanted to argue, but honestly, she sounded right.\n\nThe next morning, I tried to follow Mama Susan’s words. I walked a quick pace around the dusty field while the sun was just warming the roofs. It was harder than my normal slow stroll—I was tempted to give up and just greet my neighbour, but I remembered the big event coming next month. How will I lift those tents and tables if I can’t handle a short walk today? So I pushed myself, sweating and breathing deep, even if my muscles complained.\n\nSlowly, my body started to feel the difference. My breathing got easier. And when the bigger event came, I carried not just one, but two big benches, helping others and laughing along. I realised that a small change—just 30 minutes five days a week—protected me from feeling weak again. Now, when people ask how to stay fit, I tell them, ‘Just start, you will see the benefits soon. No more easy problems becoming big crises in my life!’	{https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/f95ac8d0-1c63-4f02-a24b-86bb2ff80cc7_0.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/f95ac8d0-1c63-4f02-a24b-86bb2ff80cc7_1.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/f95ac8d0-1c63-4f02-a24b-86bb2ff80cc7_2.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/f95ac8d0-1c63-4f02-a24b-86bb2ff80cc7_3.png}	{https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/f95ac8d0-1c63-4f02-a24b-86bb2ff80cc7_0.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/f95ac8d0-1c63-4f02-a24b-86bb2ff80cc7_1.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/f95ac8d0-1c63-4f02-a24b-86bb2ff80cc7_2.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/f95ac8d0-1c63-4f02-a24b-86bb2ff80cc7_3.mp3}	How often and how long should I exercise to actually improve my health?	exercise	male	independent	2026-02-24 14:11:15.117638+00	\N
