th limited support at home?&quot;,\n  &quot;Are there local herbal or traditional remedies commonly used in the Luo community of Kisumu for managing hypertension or diabetes, and are they safe?&quot;,\n  &quot;How can farming and animal keeping be integrated into an active routine to improve health for older women with type 2 diabetes in Kisumu?&quot;,\n  &quot;What precautions should older women with hypertension and diabetes take when getting insulin injections or oral medications in urban Kenyan clinics?&quot;,\n  &quot;How often should someone with easy access to healthy foods in Kisumu snack if they have type 2 diabetes and are on a lactose-free diet?&quot;,\n  &quot;Are there success stories or local initiatives for female fish traders in Kisumu adopting lifestyle changes for better diabetes management?&quot;\n]</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">Category</td>\n                <td class="p-2">diet</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">study_number</td>\n                <td class="p-2">d8f3139f-b56b-485c-98ad-7e516daf73d4</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">health_goals</td>\n                <td class="p-2">Which everyday foods can I eat that won&#x27;t make my blood sugar spike?</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">output_format</td>\n                <td class="p-2">Text, Image and audio</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">type</td>\n                <td class="p-2">overlapped</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">parent</td>\n                <td class="p-2"></td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">label</td>\n                <td class="p-2">EXCELLENT</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">story_arc</td>\n                <td class="p-2">social_support</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">output_tone</td>\n                <td class="p-2">social_support</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n                </tbody>\n            </table>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n     \n    <style>\n            .guideline-html-content h1 {\n                font-size: 1.1rem;\n                font-weight: 800;\n                margin-bottom: 0.5rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h2 {\n                font-size: 1rem;\n                font-weight: 700;\n                margin-bottom: 0.4rem;\n                margin-top: 1rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h3 {\n                font-size: 0.9rem;\n                font-weight: 600;\n                margin-bottom: 0.3rem;\n                margin-top: 0.8rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content p {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content ul,\n            .guideline-html-content ol {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n                padding-left: 1.25rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content li {\n                margin-bottom: 0.2rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content strong {\n                font-weight: 700;\n                color: #1e293b;\n            }\n        </style> </div> 	You see, for me, every morning starts before the sun comes up. I pack some sweet mandazi and a flask of milky chai, then hurry to Kibuye market to open my fish stall. Who has time to wonder if that chapati and tea is not the best for sugar, when so many customers and fish are waiting? Today, as usual, I ate my fried bread and sweet tea quickly before starting to sort omena for packing into small bags. But before I finished the last sack, I felt so dizzy and shaky, I nearly dropped my scale! You ever felt like your own body is betraying you just when you need it most?\n\nThat is when Nurse Atieno from the local clinic passed by for her usual market rounds. She found me sitting under my umbrella looking confused, and asked gently if I measured my blood sugar after breakfast. I almost pretended I was fine, but she knows me too well. "Achieng, your body is calling for help. Try eating boiled sweet potatoes or groundnuts instead, and drink water or unsweetened tea. They will not push your sugar up too fast, and you will stay strong till midday." I wanted to argue—how can tea without sugar taste like anything?—but the way she spoke softly and confidently made me feel she truly cared. I promised to try, even if I feared I would miss my sweet morning treat.\n\nWhen I reached home that evening, I decided to prepare what Nurse Atieno suggested. I boiled some sweet potatoes, roasted a small handful of groundnuts, and cut up some fresh guava for tomorrow. The next morning, I felt nervous—a bit lost without my sweet tea and mandazi. Old habits, eh? And sure enough, I nearly slipped and poured hot water on my hand! But I remembered I had a big order coming for fresh tilapia tomorrow. If I want to be strong for that, I must try. So I put a brave face, ate the sweet potato, chewed the groundnuts, and sipped my plain tea slowly, watching the sunrise over the lake.\n\nAfter a few days, you know what happened? My hands stopped shaking, even as the market work grew busy. I could pack more omena, greet customers with a smile, and my headaches became less. Today, when the restaurant owner picked up his bulk order, I stood taller than usual and thanked God for the strength to finish. I still miss my sweet treats sometimes, but now, every time I choose groundnuts instead, I feel like I am giving myself more chances—not just for a better market day, but for many good days ahead. If I can do this, slowly, anyone can.	{https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/d8f3139f-b56b-485c-98ad-7e516daf73d4_0.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/d8f3139f-b56b-485c-98ad-7e516daf73d4_1.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/d8f3139f-b56b-485c-98ad-7e516daf73d4_2.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/d8f3139f-b56b-485c-98ad-7e516daf73d4_3.png}	{https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/d8f3139f-b56b-485c-98ad-7e516daf73d4_0.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/d8f3139f-b56b-485c-98ad-7e516daf73d4_1.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/d8f3139f-b56b-485c-98ad-7e516daf73d4_2.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/d8f3139f-b56b-485c-98ad-7e516daf73d4_3.mp3}	Which everyday foods can I eat that won't make my blood sugar spike?	diet	female	overlapped	2026-02-24 14:11:13.196808+00	\N
