</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">alcohol</td>\n                <td class="p-2">No</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">physical_activity</td>\n                <td class="p-2">3-4 days</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">diet_restrictions</td>\n                <td class="p-2">Gluten-Free</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">support_network</td>\n                <td class="p-2">Community or religious group</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">Question</td>\n                <td class="p-2">Can you give me some simple meal ideas or a sample daily menu I could follow?</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">generated_queries</td>\n                <td class="p-2">[\n  &quot;What are affordable Halal meal options using local ingredients available in Homa Bay for someone managing type 2 diabetes?&quot;,\n  &quot;How can I balance my Luo cultural dishes with a diabetes-friendly diet while living in a suburban area near Homa Bay town?&quot;,\n  &quot;Are there community exercise groups or Ohangla dance classes in Homa Bay that welcome women in their late 20s to early 30s?&quot;,\n  &quot;What support do local healthcare clinics in Homa Bay offer for diabetes education for young female transport operators like me?&quot;,\n  &quot;How can I find healthy, budget-friendly recipes using commonly found foods in Homa Bay supermarkets or markets?&quot;,\n  &quot;Is it safe for someone on insulin and oral medication to smoke tobacco weekly, and what are the local resources in Homa Bay to help quit smoking?&quot;,\n  &quot;Where can I buy low-cost, fresh vegetables and fruits in the suburbs near Homa Bay town with easy access to public transportation?&quot;,\n  &quot;How can I fit regular physical activity, like dancing Ohangla, into my busy routine as a female transport operator in Kenya?&quot;,\n  &quot;Are there any local Luo traditional foods that are Halal and suitable for people with type 2 diabetes?&quot;,\n  &quot;What community or religious groups in Homa Bay provide support for agnostic women with diabetes who don&#x27;t consume alcohol?&quot;,\n  &quot;How do seasonal changes in Homa Bay affect the availability and prices of healthy foods, and how can I adjust my diet accordingly?&quot;,\n  &quot;What are some strategies for eating healthy on a budget in Homa Bay when you have easy access to healthy foods but limited finances?&quot;\n]</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">Category</td>\n                <td class="p-2">diet</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">study_number</td>\n                <td class="p-2">7bedc749-a2b9-4cf9-80e5-a980d953f944</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">health_goals</td>\n                <td class="p-2">Can you give me some simple meal ideas or a sample daily menu I could follow?</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">output_format</td>\n                <td class="p-2">Text, Image and audio</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">type</td>\n                <td class="p-2">overlapped</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">parent</td>\n                <td class="p-2"></td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">label</td>\n                <td class="p-2">EXCELLENT</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">story_arc</td>\n                <td class="p-2">social_support</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">output_tone</td>\n                <td class="p-2">social_support</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n                </tbody>\n            </table>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n     \n    <style>\n            .guideline-html-content h1 {\n                font-size: 1.1rem;\n                font-weight: 800;\n                margin-bottom: 0.5rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h2 {\n                font-size: 1rem;\n                font-weight: 700;\n                margin-bottom: 0.4rem;\n                margin-top: 1rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h3 {\n                font-size: 0.9rem;\n                font-weight: 600;\n                margin-bottom: 0.3rem;\n                margin-top: 0.8rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content p {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content ul,\n            .guideline-html-content ol {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n                padding-left: 1.25rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content li {\n                margin-bottom: 0.2rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content strong {\n                font-weight: 700;\n                color: #1e293b;\n            }\n        </style> </div> 	Every morning in Homa Bay I wake up, fix a quick cup of tea, and rush out, always thinking, 'Will I have enough passengers today?' Being a transport operator, time is money, and so my breakfast is just a slice of white bread and tea with lots of sugar—no time for more. I pack fried chips or mandazi for lunch, thinking these foods are quick and filling for a busy day. But last week, after a rushed lunch and a busy shift, my hands started shaking while I was arranging boarding for my customers. Eish, how did I even forget my meds? Because of that, I lost three passengers to the next matatu, just because I felt weak and slow to collect fares. Have you ever felt like your own body is fighting your job?\n\nThe next day, I decided to visit the clinic near the market where a nurse called Maureen always greets people like we're her sisters. I thought, 'Will she just tell me to eat less and exercise more?' Instead, she sat me down, smiled, and said, 'Listen, Achieng, with your work and diabetes, you have to plan your meals just like you plan your routes—start with what is fresh and cheap in the market! Swap white bread and mandazi for boiled sweet potatoes, brown ugali with sukuma wiki, and roasted fish. Carry fruit like guava, not bananas. You’ll have more energy and you won’t be scrambling for your meds.' The advice made sense, but I wasn’t sure I could change so much. Still, I promised to try.\n\nThat afternoon, I tried boiling sweet potatoes at home for the next day and packed sukuma and tilapia in a sufuria. But waking up early and preparing these meals wasn’t easy—my fingers wanted to grab that slice of bread or buy chips on the road. On the second morning, I nearly forgot my lunch at home! I chased my little brother to bring it to the matatu stage. Chai! I was embarrassed, but I remembered I had a big contracting trip with more passengers at the end of the week. That thought kept me going. I told myself, 'If you can manage this routine for one week, you can handle anything.'\n\nBy the end of the week, I noticed I was feeling lighter and less tired. My mind was sharper and my sugar levels stayed steady through the workday. When Friday’s big contracting job came, I finished my day smoothly—even had time to join a quick Ohangla dance with other operators during lunch! Now, I'm thinking, maybe with small changes and help from people like Nurse Maureen, I can actually do more. Who knew just switching food could help me not just work better but also enjoy life with more energy?	{https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/7bedc749-a2b9-4cf9-80e5-a980d953f944_0.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/7bedc749-a2b9-4cf9-80e5-a980d953f944_1.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/7bedc749-a2b9-4cf9-80e5-a980d953f944_2.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/7bedc749-a2b9-4cf9-80e5-a980d953f944_3.png}	{https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/7bedc749-a2b9-4cf9-80e5-a980d953f944_0.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/7bedc749-a2b9-4cf9-80e5-a980d953f944_1.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/7bedc749-a2b9-4cf9-80e5-a980d953f944_2.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/7bedc749-a2b9-4cf9-80e5-a980d953f944_3.mp3}	Can you give me some simple meal ideas or a sample daily menu I could follow?	diet	female	overlapped	2026-02-24 14:11:13.533123+00	\N
