e or vigorous exercise for diabetes management, especially for young female adults?&quot;,\n  &quot;What herbal or traditional medicines used by the Luo community are safe to combine with insulin or metformin for diabetes?&quot;,\n  &quot;How accessible and reliable is diabetes care at local clinics or hospitals in Homa Bay for young adults without family support?&quot;,\n  &quot;Are there local fitness facilities or outdoor spaces near Homa Bay where women can exercise safely five to seven days a week?&quot;,\n  &quot;What cultural festivals or community events around Homa Bay feature physical activities or traditional dances compatible with a diabetic lifestyle?&quot;\n]</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">Category</td>\n                <td class="p-2">diet</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">study_number</td>\n                <td class="p-2">a942fa3c-e898-4d5e-b79f-dd38083e3ac4</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">health_goals</td>\n                <td class="p-2">Can you give me some simple meal ideas or a sample daily menu I could follow?</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">output_format</td>\n                <td class="p-2">Text, Image and audio</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">type</td>\n                <td class="p-2">control</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">parent</td>\n                <td class="p-2"></td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">label</td>\n                <td class="p-2">EXCELLENT</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">story_arc</td>\n                <td class="p-2">resistance</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">output_tone</td>\n                <td class="p-2">resistance</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n                </tbody>\n            </table>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n     \n    <style>\n            .guideline-html-content h1 {\n                font-size: 1.1rem;\n                font-weight: 800;\n                margin-bottom: 0.5rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h2 {\n                font-size: 1rem;\n                font-weight: 700;\n                margin-bottom: 0.4rem;\n                margin-top: 1rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h3 {\n                font-size: 0.9rem;\n                font-weight: 600;\n                margin-bottom: 0.3rem;\n                margin-top: 0.8rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content p {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content ul,\n            .guideline-html-content ol {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n                padding-left: 1.25rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content li {\n                margin-bottom: 0.2rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content strong {\n                font-weight: 700;\n                color: #1e293b;\n            }\n        </style> </div> 	Every morning before sunrise, I Achieng Otieno, grab my fishing basket and hurry down towards Lake Victoria, just like I've done nearly every day since I finished school. I always rush breakfast – sometimes it's leftover white maize ugali or tea and mandazi from the duka. Don’t we all think we are still strong enough for anything? Today, I skipped packing any snacks into my bag, saying to myself, "I'll just eat after work." Halfway through casting my nets, my hands shook and sweat dripped from my brow, but I thought it was just the sun being too hot. By lunchtime, I was so dizzy I couldn’t even help my neighbour untangle his net, and he had to finish the job for me.\n\nLater that afternoon, when I dragged myself to the local clinic, the nurse shook her head. She said, “Achieng, we’ve talked—your blood sugar is falling because you’re skipping proper meals and snacks. Let’s make it easy. In your market, you’ll always find millet or sorghum flour—make kuon using that, eat with omena stew or tilapia wet fry and mboga, maybe throw in tomatoes and onions for kachumbari. Carry roasted groundnuts or fresh fruit for a snack. These foods keep your energy up and your blood sugar steady till evening. No need to change everything at once, just start small.” I nodded but still wondered—must I really fuss so much just for food?\n\nNext morning, I tried her advice, feeling almost silly cooking millet ugali and putting omena into a plastic container for later. It's strange how hard it is to break a habit, huh? At the lake, I nearly forgot my meal until my phone alarm beeped. All the other fishers laughed, saying, 'Achieng, since when do you eat like an elder?' Still, I munched on groundnuts, took a deep breath and went back to hauling the net. My hands shook less, but changing routine felt awkward. I wanted to give up, but tomorrow was the big community clean-up at the fish market—how could I miss that?\n\nWith each day, following the new meal pattern grew a bit easier. During the clean-up, I moved quickly, lifting crates and joining in an Ohangla dance at lunch because my energy held steady. That evening, as I watched the sun set over Lake Victoria, I felt proud—could taking care of myself actually help me do more? Maybe I’ll stick to this, try new recipes, and keep dancing. If my health keeps improving bit by bit, maybe I’ll become the one everybody in the market asks for advice, not just for fish, but food too.	{https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/a942fa3c-e898-4d5e-b79f-dd38083e3ac4_0.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/a942fa3c-e898-4d5e-b79f-dd38083e3ac4_1.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/a942fa3c-e898-4d5e-b79f-dd38083e3ac4_2.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/a942fa3c-e898-4d5e-b79f-dd38083e3ac4_3.png}	{https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/a942fa3c-e898-4d5e-b79f-dd38083e3ac4_0.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/a942fa3c-e898-4d5e-b79f-dd38083e3ac4_1.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/a942fa3c-e898-4d5e-b79f-dd38083e3ac4_2.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/a942fa3c-e898-4d5e-b79f-dd38083e3ac4_3.mp3}	Can you give me some simple meal ideas or a sample daily menu I could follow?	diet	female	control	2026-02-24 14:11:17.118785+00	\N
