        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">occupation</td>\n                <td class="p-2">Radio presenter</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">daily_routine</td>\n                <td class="p-2">Working adult</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">hobbies</td>\n                <td class="p-2">Swimming</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">activities</td>\n                <td class="p-2">Exercise or physical activities</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">health_conditions</td>\n                <td class="p-2">Hypertension (high blood pressure)</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">medication</td>\n                <td class="p-2">Insulin injections, Oral medication (e.g., Metformin), Lifestyle changes only (no medication), Herbal or traditional medicine</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">healthcare_resources</td>\n                <td class="p-2">Local healthcare clinic or hospital</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">healthcare_access</td>\n                <td class="p-2">Yes</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">healthcare_frequency</td>\n                <td class="p-2">Regularly (at least once a year)</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">culture</td>\n                <td class="p-2">Luo</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">t2d_status</td>\n                <td class="p-2">Yes</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">tobacco</td>\n                <td class="p-2">Yes</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">alcohol</td>\n                <td class="p-2">Yes</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">physical_activity</td>\n                <td class="p-2">3-4 days</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">diet_restrictions</td>\n                <td class="p-2">Kosher</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">support_network</td>\n                <td class="p-2">Healthcare provider or counsellor</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">Question</td>\n                <td class="p-2">Eating healthy can get expensive—how can I manage a nutritious diet on a tight budget? And can I still enjoy some traditional foods? </td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">generated_queries</td>\n                <td class="p-2">[\n  &quot;What are some vegetarian-friendly, healthy Kenyan snack options available in urban areas of Homa Bay for managing type 2 diabetes and hypertension?&quot;,\n  &quot;How does the Luo culture influence vegetarian dietary practices for women aged 55-64 with diabetes in Homa Bay, Kenya?&quot;,\n  &quot;What local Luo or Kenyan herbal or traditional medicines are commonly used alongside prescribed diabetes medication, and are they safe to combine for someone like me with hypertension?&quot;,\n  &quot;Are there public swimming pools or safe swimming facilities in Homa Bay city where women over 55 can exercise regularly?&quot;,\n  &quot;As a Presbyterian Christian living in urban Kenya, are there any church or community groups in Homa Bay that support diabetes management or healthy lifestyle activities?&quot;,\n  &quot;What culturally relevant exercise routines are recommended for Luo women over 55 to help manage diabetes and high blood pressure in an urban Kenyan setting?&quot;,\n  &quot;Which local vegetarian dishes or snacks available in Homa Bay markets are suitable for someone managing diabetes and trying to avoid high blood pressure?&quot;,\n  &quot;How can a working radio presenter with a busy routine in Homa Bay effectively schedule physical activity 3-4 days a week, considering dietary and health restrictions?&quot;,\n  &quot;What are the safest and healthiest options for Luo women in Homa Bay who occasionally consume alcohol or tobacco but want to minimize impact on diabetes and hypertension?&quot;,\n  &quot;How often should a diabetic with hypertension aged 55-64 have healthy snacks between meals to maintain stable blood sugar levels, in the context of Kenyan dietary habits?&quot;,\n  &quot;What resources or support networks are available at local healthcare clinics in Homa Bay for women with type 2 diabetes following a vegetarian diet?&quot;,\n  &quot;Can you suggest swimming-based exercise routines suitable for older Kenyan women with diabetes, focusing on safety and health goals in an urban Homa Bay environment?&quot;\n]</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">Category</td>\n                <td class="p-2">diet</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">study_number</td>\n                <td class="p-2">a986a2e0-d731-4795-ad57-d3c91a0890af</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">health_goals</td>\n                <td class="p-2">Eating healthy can get expensive—how can I manage a nutritious diet on a tight budget? And can I still enjoy some traditional foods? </td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">output_format</td>\n                <td class="p-2">Text, Image and audio</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">type</td>\n                <td class="p-2">independent</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">parent</td>\n                <td class="p-2"></td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">label</td>\n                <td class="p-2">BAD</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">story_arc</td>\n                <td class="p-2">classic_change</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n            <tr>\n                <td class="p-2 font-bold">output_tone</td>\n                <td class="p-2">classic_change</td>\n            </tr>\n        \n                </tbody>\n            </table>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n     \n    <style>\n            .guideline-html-content h1 {\n                font-size: 1.1rem;\n                font-weight: 800;\n                margin-bottom: 0.5rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h2 {\n                font-size: 1rem;\n                font-weight: 700;\n                margin-bottom: 0.4rem;\n                margin-top: 1rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content h3 {\n                font-size: 0.9rem;\n                font-weight: 600;\n                margin-bottom: 0.3rem;\n                margin-top: 0.8rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content p {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content ul,\n            .guideline-html-content ol {\n                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;\n                padding-left: 1.25rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content li {\n                margin-bottom: 0.2rem;\n            }\n\n            .guideline-html-content strong {\n                font-weight: 700;\n                color: #1e293b;\n            }\n        </style> </div> 	You know, every weekday morning I wake up to the busy sounds of Homa Bay town. My radio show starts early, and that means I have to get ready quickly. Sometimes, I just grab a slice of white bread, maybe a sausage if I’m lucky, and dash out the door. Who has time to prepare fancy food when listeners are waiting? One day, my boss asked me to read the news summary for the prime hour—a small but important task. But just as I went live, I felt dizzy and my words jumbled. I tried to smile, but inside, I thought: can skipping a good breakfast really mess up my whole day?\n\nLater that afternoon, I went to the local clinic for my insulin shot. The nurse, Mary, noticed I looked tired. She asked if I was eating well, so I said, 'Healthy eating is expensive, and I can’t always avoid mandazi and samosas.' Mary just smiled and showed me how affordable healthy foods can be. She wrote down simple meal ideas: ugali made with whole grain flour, sukuma wiki with onions and tomatoes, kidney beans, and fruits from the market. ‘Tradition doesn’t mean unhealthy, Achieng,’ she told me. ‘Try swapping just one thing each week. Your body—and your listeners—will thank you.’ I listened, but part of me wondered if small changes could really make a big difference.\n\nThe next day, I tried Mary’s advice. It wasn’t easy! I almost gave up when the smell of chips from the street called my name. But I thought about my next big show—an outdoor health event I was hosting soon. I knew I had to stay sharp and healthy. So, I bought sukuma wiki, cooked it quickly, and made ugali with just a bit of margarine. When my friends laughed and waved their sodas at me, I almost gave in, but I remembered the nurse’s words. Can one choice lead to many good tomorrows?\n\nWith time, switching up my meals got easier. I added groundnuts and enjoyed fruit juices with little sugar. By the day of the outdoor broadcast, I felt light, strong, and proud. My words came out clear and my voice was lively—no dizziness at all! Afterward, I shared my journey on air, and listeners called in with their own stories. Now, I know that eating well on a budget is not just possible; it’s powerful. Every day, I find new ways to balance tradition and health, becoming more confident to inspire others. Maybe, just maybe, this journey is just getting started?	{https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/a986a2e0-d731-4795-ad57-d3c91a0890af_0.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/a986a2e0-d731-4795-ad57-d3c91a0890af_1.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/a986a2e0-d731-4795-ad57-d3c91a0890af_2.png,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/official/a986a2e0-d731-4795-ad57-d3c91a0890af_3.png}	{https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/a986a2e0-d731-4795-ad57-d3c91a0890af_0.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/a986a2e0-d731-4795-ad57-d3c91a0890af_1.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/a986a2e0-d731-4795-ad57-d3c91a0890af_2.mp3,https://prxquaevkggpwryikieg.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/audios/official/a986a2e0-d731-4795-ad57-d3c91a0890af_3.mp3}	Eating healthy can get expensive—how can I manage a nutritious diet on a tight budget? And can I still enjoy some traditional foods? 	diet	female	independent	2026-02-24 14:11:17.380581+00	\N
